{id:'panormos',name:'Panormos Beach',loc:'Skopelos, Sporades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered bay on the island of Skopelos',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.1108,lng:23.6536,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A sheltered bay on the west coast of Skopelos with calm water, pine-covered hills and a small strip of sand and pebbles.',fac:'Tavernas and some sunbeds nearby; check locally',park:'Roadside parking close to the beach; check locally',tip:'Boat trips and water sports run from the bay in summer. Calm conditions make it good for families.'},
{id:'megaliammos',name:'Megali Ammos',loc:'Skiathos, Sporades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Town bay with calm water and tavernas',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:39.1601,lng:23.482,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A sandy bay a short distance from Skiathos town, with shallow, calm water and a line of tavernas along the waterfront.',fac:'Tavernas, sunbeds and water sports; check locally',park:'Limited parking nearby; check locally',tip:'Busy in high season, so arrive early for a spot near the water.'},
{id:'mitjana',name:'Cala Mitjana',loc:'Ciutadella, Menorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Pine-framed cove on Menorca south coast',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.9331,lng:3.9736,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#e6e0d0'],desc:'A small, sheltered cove of white sand and clear turquoise water, framed by pine trees and low cliffs on the south coast of Menorca.',fac:'No facilities on the beach; bring water and shade',park:'Car park a walk from the cove; check locally',tip:'Reached on foot through the pinewoods. It fills quickly in high season, so go early.'},
{id:'mingardo',name:'Mingardo Beach',loc:'Marina di Camerota, Campania',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble cove below Capo Palinuro cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:40.0324,lng:15.3208,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#c9c2b2'],desc:'A quiet cove of small pebbles and clear water on the Cilento coast, set between green cliffs near Marina di Camerota.',fac:'Small seasonal facilities; check locally',park:'Parking above the cove with a walk down; check locally',tip:'Take care on the path down, and conditions can change with the sea. Bring water and shade.'},
{id:'lone',name:'Lone Bay',loc:'Rovinj, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pine-shaded pebble bay near Rovinj',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:45.0689,lng:13.6338,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A pebble and rock bay with clear water, shaded by pines in the Zlatni Rt forest park just south of Rovinj, with paths along the coast.',fac:'Cafes, sunbeds and a promenade nearby; check locally',park:'Car parks near the park, often busy in summer; check locally',tip:'Water shoes help on the pebbles. The bay is lovely at sunset, so consider an evening visit.'},
{id:'nugal',name:'Nugal Beach',loc:'Makarska, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Hidden pebble cove under limestone cliffs',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:43.2825,lng:17.034,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#e6e0d0'],desc:'A small, secluded pebble cove with clear turquoise water below limestone cliffs and pines, reached on foot along a path from the Makarska coast.',fac:'No facilities; bring water and shade',park:'Parking in town and a walk along the coastal path; check locally',tip:'Often used by naturists, so expect clothing-optional visitors. The path is rough, so wear sturdy shoes.'},
{id:'formentor',name:'Formentor Beach',loc:'Pollensa, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Turquoise bay at the end of the Formentor road',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.929,lng:3.133,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A sheltered bay of pale sand and shallow turquoise water at the foot of the Formentor peninsula in northern Mallorca, backed by pine trees.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds and a nearby hotel; check locally',park:'Car park near the beach; the Formentor road is busy in summer; check locally',tip:'The road to Formentor can have traffic limits in peak season, so check current rules and go early.'},
{id:'santacruz',name:'Praia de Santa Cruz',loc:'Torres Vedras, Estremadura',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Atlantic beach with sea stacks',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.134,lng:-9.384,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A wide Atlantic beach of golden sand with dramatic rock stacks, popular with surfers and known for its golden evening light.',fac:'Cafes, a surf school and sunbeds in season; check locally',park:'Parking near the beach; check locally',tip:'Atlantic swell and currents can be strong. Swim only in lifeguarded areas.'},
{id:'gravette',name:'Plage de la Gravette',loc:'Antibes, French Riviera',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Town beach beside the old port of Antibes',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:43.58,lng:7.128,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small sandy beach right beside the old town and port of Antibes, with calm shallow water and a walk to the ramparts.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants in the old town; check locally',park:'Public car parks near the port; check locally',tip:'Busy in summer because it is so central. Go early for space on the sand.'},
{id:'triopetra',name:'Triopetra Beach',loc:'Rethymno, South Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long south-coast beach with three rock formations',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:35.1208,lng:24.5453,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long, quiet beach of sand and fine pebbles on the south coast of Crete, named for the three rock formations standing in the water. Calmer and less visited than the big north-coast resorts.',fac:'A few tavernas nearby; sunbeds in places; check locally',park:'Roadside and small car parks near the village; check locally',tip:'The south coast can be windy. Check the wind forecast and bring water and shade.'},
{id:'xigia',name:'Xigia Beach',loc:'Zakynthos, Ionian Islands',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'rocky',tag:'Sulphur springs and turquoise water under pale cliffs',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.89,lng:20.75,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small sandy and rocky cove on the north-east coast of Zakynthos, known for its sulphur springs, cloudy-turquoise water and pale cliffs. Popular with boat trips as well as visitors by road.',fac:'Seasonal snack bar and sunbeds; check locally',park:'Small car park above the beach; check locally',tip:'The sulphur water has a strong smell by design. Go early to avoid the boat-trip crowds.'},
{id:'monachile',name:'Lama Monachile',loc:'Polignano a Mare, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble cove squeezed between white cliffs and the old town',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:40.9969,lng:17.2236,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small pebble cove at the foot of Polignano a Mare, framed by tall limestone cliffs and houses built right at the edge. Clear, deep water close to shore and a short walk from the old town.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants in the old town above; check locally',park:'Paid car parks on the edge of town, then a short walk; check locally',tip:'Very small and crowded in summer. Go early or in the evening, and wear water shoes for the pebbles.'},
{id:'piscinas',name:'Spiaggia di Piscinas',loc:'Arbus, Costa Verde, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Giant golden dunes on the Costa Verde',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.5483,lng:8.4538,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A wild, long beach backed by some of the tallest sand dunes in Europe, on the Costa Verde of south-west Sardinia. Open, quiet and a long way from the resort strips.',fac:'A seasonal bar or snack stand near the beach; otherwise very few facilities',park:'Parking near the beach reached by a long unpaved road; check locally',tip:'The road in is rough and there is little shade. Bring water, sun protection and shoes for hot sand.'},
{id:'albandeira',name:'Praia da Albandeira',loc:'Lagoa, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Small sandy cove under golden Algarve cliffs',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:37.0911,lng:-8.3998,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small, sheltered cove at the foot of golden limestone cliffs in the Algarve, with a natural rock arch and clear water. Reached by a short path and steps from the clifftop.',fac:'A seasonal snack bar at the top of the steps; check locally',park:'Free car park at the clifftop; check locally',tip:'Go early or late in summer to avoid crowds. The steps down can be steep, so wear sturdy shoes.'},
{id:'sotavento',name:'Playa de Sotavento',loc:'Jandia, Fuerteventura',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Turquoise lagoon and long sandbar on Fuerteventura',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:28.1089,lng:-14.2339,season:'April&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A very long beach of pale sand on the south of Fuerteventura, with a shallow turquoise lagoon and a sandbar that changes with the tides. Wide, open and often windy.',fac:'A few beach bars and kitesurf schools along the beach; check locally',park:'Parking areas along the access roads; check locally',tip:'The wind can be strong. Check tides and wind before you go, and take sun protection as there is little shade.'},
{id:'alvor',name:'Praia de Alvor',loc:'Alvor, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sandy beach beside the Alvor estuary',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.1228,lng:-8.5946,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long, wide sandy beach next to the Alvor estuary in the western Algarve, with space to spread out and calm conditions on most summer days.',fac:'Beach cafes and restaurants nearby in Alvor; check locally',park:'Car parks near the beach and town; check locally',tip:'Plenty of space even in summer. Walk toward the estuary end for a quieter stretch.'},
{id:'meco',name:'Praia do Meco',loc:'Sesimbra, Lisbon coast',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Atlantic beach south of Lisbon with big waves',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.4742,lng:-9.1814,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long, open Atlantic beach on the coast south of Lisbon, backed by low cliffs, with golden sand, strong surf and a relaxed local feel.',fac:'Beach restaurants near the main access; check locally',park:'Car parks near the main access; check locally',tip:'Waves and currents can be strong, so swim only where lifeguards are on duty. Part of the beach is used by naturists.'},
{id:'seixal',name:'Praia do Seixal',loc:'Seixal, Madeira',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Black volcanic sand under green Madeira cliffs',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:32.8231,lng:-17.1098,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small beach of dark volcanic sand on the north coast of Madeira, framed by steep green cliffs. A natural sea pool and a few cafes sit nearby.',fac:'Cafes and a natural pool nearby; check locally',park:'Small car park near the beach; check locally',tip:'The Atlantic can be rough on this coast. Swim carefully and check conditions before going in.'},
{id:'tavira',name:'Ilha de Tavira',loc:'Tavira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Barrier island beach reached by a short ferry',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:37.117,lng:-7.62,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long barrier island off the eastern Algarve with wide sandy beaches, calm lagoon water on one side and the open Atlantic on the other. Reached by a short ferry or boat from Tavira.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants near the ferry landing; check locally',park:'Parking is on the mainland near the ferry; check locally',tip:'Check ferry times and last return before you go. Bring water and shade, as the island has little cover.'},
{id:'cabopino',name:'Playa de Cabopino',loc:'Marbella, Costa del Sol',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandy cove beside a marina and old watchtower',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:36.4907,lng:-4.7389,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A sandy beach on the Costa del Sol beside the small Cabopino marina and an old watchtower, backed by pine woods and dunes. Part of the beach is used by naturists.',fac:'Beach bars and restaurants near the marina; check locally',park:'Car park near the marina; check locally',tip:'Walk toward the dunes for a quieter spot. Part of the beach is used by naturists.'},
{id:'zahara',name:'Playa de Zahara de los Atunes',loc:'Zahara de los Atunes, Costa de la Luz',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach on the Costa de la Luz',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:36.1327,lng:-6.0388,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long, wide beach of fine pale sand on Spain&#39;s Atlantic coast, with big skies and strong evening light. Wind and surf can be strong on this stretch.',fac:'Beach bars and restaurants in the village; check locally',park:'Parking near the village and beach access points; check locally',tip:'The wind can be strong. Check the forecast and swim carefully in the Atlantic surf.'},
{id:'maspalomas',name:'Maspalomas Dunes',loc:'Maspalomas, Gran Canaria',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden Sahara-like dunes meeting the Atlantic',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:27.7395,lng:-15.5826,season:'Year-round',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A protected field of golden dunes at the southern tip of Gran Canaria, running down to a wide Atlantic beach. Walking through the dunes takes effort but the views are worth it.',fac:'Kiosks and beach bars along the beach edge; check locally',park:'Car parks near the lighthouse and beach access; check locally',tip:'Bring water and a hat, as there is little shade. Stay on the marked routes to protect the dunes. Parts of the beach are used by naturists.'},
{id:'canteras',name:'Playa de las Canteras',loc:'Las Palmas, Gran Canaria',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long city beach sheltered by a natural reef',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:28.1392,lng:-15.435,season:'Year-round',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A long, sheltered city beach in Las Palmas, protected by a natural offshore reef that keeps the water calm for most of the year. A promenade runs the whole length.',fac:'Cafes, restaurants and shops along the promenade',park:'Paid car parks nearby; check locally',tip:'The reef gives calm swimming, but check flags and tide levels. The quieter stretch is toward the north end.'},
{id:'cotillo',name:'El Cotillo Beach',loc:'El Cotillo, Fuerteventura',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Windy sandy beach with turquoise water and windsurfers',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:28.6837,lng:-14.0125,season:'April&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A wide sandy beach near the fishing village of El Cotillo on the north-west coast of Fuerteventura, known for clear turquoise water, steady wind and windsurfers.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants in El Cotillo village; check locally',park:'Parking near the village and beach access points; check locally',tip:'The wind is steady, so check the forecast before swimming. Some sections have rocks in the water.'},
{id:'burgau',name:'Praia de Burgau',loc:'Burgau, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Small sandy beach below a whitewashed village',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.0733,lng:-8.7745,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1f93bb','#d9d3c4'],desc:'A small sandy beach in the western Algarve, backed by the whitewashed houses of Burgau village and framed by green hills. Swimming is usually calmer than on the open west coast.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants in the village; check locally',park:'Street parking in the village and a car park nearby; check locally',tip:'The beach can be busy in July and August, so arrive early. Check sea conditions before swimming.'},
{id:'barrosa',name:'Playa de la Barrosa',loc:'Chiclana de la Frontera, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Atlantic beach with red cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:36.3547,lng:-6.1813,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a7fb8','#e0cfa8'],desc:'An 8 km sweep of fine golden sand on the Costa de la Luz, backed by pine woods and a low red cliff at the north end. At low tide the sand flats and rock pools stretch far out, and the sunsets over the Atlantic are the main event.',fac:'Chiringuitos, showers, lifeguards in season, sunbed rental on the central stretch',park:'Free and paid car parks along the promenade; fills by midday in summer',tip:'Walk north toward Sancti Petri at low tide for the quietest sand and the best light.'},
{id:'castelejo',name:'Praia do Castelejo',loc:'Vila do Bispo, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild west-coast beach under dark cliffs',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.1001,lng:-8.9455,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#2d7fb0','#cdbf9f'],desc:'A wide Atlantic beach on the wild western Algarve, set below tilted dark schist cliffs and rolling hills. Waves are strong, the water is cold and the beach stays quiet even in summer, with surfers and walkers as the main visitors.',fac:'Small beach bar in season, seasonal lifeguard, no sunbed rental',park:'Free dirt car park above the beach; short walk down',tip:'Check the swell and tide before swimming, and bring a windbreaker. Sunset is spectacular.'},
{id:'arromanches',name:'Arromanches Gold Beach',loc:'Arromanches-les-Bains, Normandy',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'D-Day beach with the Mulberry harbour remains',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:49.3395,lng:-0.62,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#6f8fa6','#d7c7a4'],desc:'A broad sandy beach below chalk cliffs, known as Gold Beach in the 1944 landings. At low tide the concrete remains of the Mulberry harbour appear offshore, and the small town behind has museums, cafes and a seafront promenade.',fac:'Cafes, restaurants, toilets and showers in town; lifeguard in July and August',park:'Paid car parks in town, a few minutes on foot from the sand',tip:'Visit at low tide to walk toward the harbour remains, and check tide times first; the sea comes in quickly.'},
{id:'arutas',name:'Is Arutas',loc:'Cabras, Sinis Peninsula, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quartz-sand beach with multicoloured grains',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:39.9513,lng:8.4015,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e8e2d0'],desc:'A beach on the Sinis peninsula in west Sardinia, known for sand made of tiny quartz grains in many colours that give the shallow water a clear, bright look. It is one of the best-known beaches of the Oristano coast.',fac:'Sunbed and umbrella rental, beach bar and showers in season',park:'Paid car park close to the sand; it fills early in summer',tip:'Arrive early in July and August. Taking sand away is banned and fined across Sardinia, so leave the quartz grains where they are.'},
{id:'barril',name:'Praia do Barril',loc:'Santa Luzia, Tavira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Ria Formosa beach with an anchor memorial',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.0853,lng:-7.6630,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#efe3c2'],desc:'A wide sandy beach on the barrier island of the Ria Formosa, reached from Santa Luzia by a flat footpath or a short tourist train. Rows of rusting anchors in the dunes behind the sand are a memorial to the local tuna fishing community.',fac:'Bars, restaurants and toilets in season, with a playground at peak times',park:'Paid car park near the start of the path in Santa Luzia',tip:'The walk takes about 15 minutes on a hard, flat path, or take the small train. Look at the anchor memorial behind the beach.'},
{id:'calahonda',name:'Playa de Calahonda',loc:'Nerja, Costa del Sol, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Town cove below the Balcon de Europa',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.7451,lng:-3.8750,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d8c9a8'],desc:'A small cove in the old town of Nerja, reached through a little arch behind the Balcon de Europa and a zigzag of steps down to the sand. Cliffs frame the beach and the cafes of the town centre are a short walk above.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, toilets and a lifeguard in high season',park:'No parking at the beach; use the town car parks and walk to the Balcon de Europa',tip:'The steps make it unsuitable for pushchairs or limited mobility. Go in the morning for more space.'},
{id:'plakias',name:'Plakias Beach',loc:'Plakias, Rethymno, Crete, Greece',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long south-coast beach with tavernas',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:35.1851,lng:24.3998,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0f7fa8','#e3cfa5'],desc:'A long sandy beach of about 1.3 km on the south coast of Crete, roughly 40 km from Rethymno. The village behind has tavernas, shops and supermarkets, and quieter stretches lie under the trees.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, tavernas, beach bars and toilets',park:'Parking in the village, with plenty of space outside peak season',tip:'Check the wind forecast, as strong wind makes the beach hard to use. A rocky cove nearby is better for snorkelling.'},
{id:'paleokastritsa',name:'Paleokastritsa Beach',loc:'Paleokastritsa, Corfu, Greece',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Cove beaches under green cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:39.6740,lng:19.7035,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#9fbf9a'],desc:'A cluster of small coves on the north-west coast of Corfu, backed by green hills and cliffs. Agios Spyridon is the main beach, and boats from the harbour run to sea caves and quieter coves.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, tavernas, showers, toilets and boat rental',park:'Paid car park behind the main beach; it fills early in summer',tip:'Tour coaches arrive from about 11am to 3pm in July and August, so go early or late in the day.'},
{id:'rossa',name:'Cala Rossa',loc:'Favignana, Egadi Islands, Sicily',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'rocky',tag:'Rocky cove with turquoise water on Favignana',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.9213,lng:12.3622,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9b97a'],desc:'A rocky cove on the island of Favignana in the Egadi Islands, with pale tufa cliffs and clear turquoise water. There is no sand, so people swim from the rocks and flat ledges.',fac:'Very few facilities; no lifeguard reported',park:'No car park at the cove; street parking nearby or come by bike',tip:'Bring water shoes and your own shade and water. A long staircase leads down to the bay, so it is not suitable for wheelchairs.'},
{id:'zarautz',name:'Playa de Zarautz',loc:'Zarautz, Gipuzkoa, Basque Country',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Basque surf beach with a promenade',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.285,lng:-2.17,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e6d3a3'],desc:'The longest beach on the Basque coast, about 2.5 km of golden sand backed by a promenade of bars and restaurants. Several surf schools are based here and the waves suit learners as well as experienced surfers.',fac:'Lifeguard, sunshade and lounger rental, toilets, showers and surf schools',park:'Parking in town, within about ten minutes on foot of the sand',tip:'Check the tide and flags before swimming, and keep clear of the surf zones marked for boards.'},
{id:'tarida',name:'Cala Tarida',loc:'Sant Josep, Ibiza, Balearic Islands',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'West-coast Ibiza cove famous for sunsets',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.9401,lng:1.2358,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A west-facing bay on Ibiza with clear water and a curve of sand, popular for evening sunsets. Beach bars and restaurants sit on and above the beach.',fac:'Beach bars and restaurants, sunbed and parasol hire',park:'Small car park above the beach; the access road backs up by early afternoon in summer',tip:'Arrive early to find parking, and stay for sunset when the beach is calmer than the big resorts nearby.'},
{id:'carcavelos',name:'Praia de Carcavelos',loc:'Carcavelos, Cascais, Lisbon coast',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Big sandy surf beach near Lisbon',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.6785,lng:-9.333,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e8d4a0'],desc:'A wide sandy beach on the Lisbon-Cascais coast, backed by a promenade. Surf schools run lessons here and the beach is reached by train from central Lisbon.',fac:'Lifeguards in season, surf schools, toilets and showers, cafes along the promenade',park:'Free and paid parking nearby, which fills quickly on summer weekends',tip:'Take the train from Cais do Sodre to Carcavelos station (about 26 minutes) and walk to the sand, which avoids the summer parking queue.'},
{id:'aiguablava',name:'Aiguablava Beach',loc:'Begur, Costa Brava, Catalonia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Small cove below the Parador on the Costa Brava',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:41.9341,lng:3.2161,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d8c9a6'],desc:'A small sheltered cove near Begur on the Costa Brava, with pine-covered cliffs and clear water. The Parador de Aiguablava stands on the cliff above the beach.',fac:'Toilets, adapted showers, water sports and a summer beach restaurant',park:'Car park beside the Parador, paid in summer',tip:'Arrive early in July and August, as the cove is small and fills quickly.'},
{id:'agiofili',name:'Agiofili Beach',loc:'Vasiliki, Lefkada, Greece',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered Lefkada beach near Vasiliki',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.6054,lng:20.6129,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0f7fa8','#e3cfa5'],desc:'A beach about 2 km from Vasiliki on the south of Lefkada, with clear water and a sandy shore below dry hills. It is reached by road or by boat taxi from the village.',fac:'Kiosk, toilets and showers near the car park; limited food, so bring your own',park:'Paid car park before the beach gate; rates vary by season',tip:'Come early in high season and bring food and shade, as there is no taverna close by.'},
{id:'kamari',name:'Kamari Beach',loc:'Kamari, Santorini, Cyclades, Greece',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Long black-sand beach with a seafront promenade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.3731,lng:25.4826,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#334155','#94a3b8'],desc:'A long beach of dark volcanic sand and pebbles on the east coast of Santorini, backed by a seafront strip of hotels, cafes and tavernas. Sunbeds and umbrellas line most of the shore.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, lifeguard in summer, toilets, showers, tavernas and cafes',park:'Several free car parks near the beach',tip:'The dark sand gets very hot at midday, so bring waterproof sandals and arrive early for sunbeds.'},
{id:'kleftiko',name:'Kleftiko',loc:'Milos, Cyclades, Greece',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'rocky',tag:'White sea caves and arches reached by boat',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:36.6522,lng:24.333,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e5e7eb'],desc:'A cluster of white rock arches, caves and sheltered coves on the south-west coast of Milos, once used as a pirate hideout. There is no road and no beach facilities, so you swim and snorkel from a boat.',fac:'None on land; boat tours provide water, snacks and snorkel gear',park:'Not applicable; reached only by boat from Adamas or Agia Kiriaki',tip:'Book a half-day boat tour with a swim stop of an hour or more. Routes can change with strong north winds.'},
{id:'montegordo',name:'Praia de Monte Gordo',loc:'Monte Gordo, Vila Real de Santo Antonio, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide shallow beach on the eastern Algarve',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.1767,lng:-7.4435,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#efe3c2'],desc:'A broad, gently sloping beach on the eastern Algarve with shallow water, long sand and a Blue Flag. A promenade runs behind it with restaurants and shops.',fac:'Lifeguards in summer, sunbed rental, toilets and showers on the promenade, restaurants',park:'Free and paid parking nearby; busy at peak times',tip:'Arrive early in July and August for parking, and expect to pay roughly 15 to 20 euros for a set of loungers and an umbrella.'},
{id:'salines',name:'Ses Salines',loc:'Sant Josep, Ibiza, Balearic Islands',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandy beach in a natural park with beach clubs',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.8411,lng:1.3919,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A long sandy beach at the southern tip of Ibiza, inside the Ses Salines natural park with dunes and pine woods behind. Beach clubs and bars line parts of the sand.',fac:'Loungers and parasols, beach clubs, bars and restaurants',park:'Small free lot by the road that fills early; larger paid car park near the roundabout',tip:'Beach clubs can be pricey, so walk along the sand to find a quieter stretch. Summer buses run from Ibiza Town.'},
{id:'paraggi',name:'Paraggi Beach',loc:'Paraggi, Santa Margherita Ligure, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Small Portofino-coast bay of sand and fine pebbles',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:44.3108,lng:9.2087,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d9c9a3'],desc:'A small sheltered bay on the Portofino coast, framed by pastel houses and wooded hills. A free public stretch sits in the middle of the beach, with paid lidos at either end.',fac:'Paid lidos with sunbeds and cafes; a small free section; limited facilities on the free sand',park:'Parking is scarce and expensive; the coast path from Santa Margherita takes about 30 minutes',tip:'Bring your own towel and umbrella for the free section, as lido sunbeds are very expensive here.'},
{id:'baleal',name:'Praia do Baleal',loc:'Baleal, Peniche, Centro, Portugal',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered surf beaches around a small island',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.3655,lng:-9.3419,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#ead9a8'],desc:'Two sheltered beaches around the small headland of Baleal near Peniche. The north-facing side is about 800 m long and a small island to the west shelters it from the biggest swells, so it suits learners.',fac:'Many surf schools and camps, beach bars and surf shops',park:'Parking around Baleal bay and along the road, plus a car park by the cafe at nearby Supertubos',tip:'Check the swell forecast before swimming, and pick the north-facing side for the calmer water and beginner surf.'},
{id:'itzurun',name:'Itzurun Beach',loc:'Zumaia, Gipuzkoa, Basque Country',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden cove beside the Zumaia flysch cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:43.3002,lng:-2.2607,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9b97a'],desc:'A golden-sand beach of about 270 m in Zumaia, backed by the layered rock cliffs of the Basque flysch coast. The surf can be heavy and low tide reveals the rock formations along the shore.',fac:'Seafront promenade and nearby cafes and shops in town',park:'Free car park on the harbour side, roughly a 15-minute walk away; street parking is limited and fills quickly on summer weekends',tip:'Visit at low tide to see the rock formations, and check tide times before walking along the shore.'},
{id:'millor',name:'Cala Millor',loc:'Sant Llorenc des Cardassar, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long family beach with a palm-lined promenade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:39.5949,lng:3.3846,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A long, wide sandy bay on the east coast of Mallorca, backed by a palm-lined promenade of restaurants and hotels. Estimates of its length range from about 1.3 km to 2 km.',fac:'Sunbed and umbrella rental, lifeguards in peak season, restaurants along the promenade',park:'Parking near the promenade, which is limited in peak season',tip:'Arrive early in July and August for parking and sunbeds, and use the promenade cycle path to reach quieter ends of the bay.'},
{id:'monterosso',name:'Monterosso al Mare',loc:'Monterosso al Mare, Cinque Terre, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Cinque Terre village beach by the train station',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:44.1451,lng:9.6472,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#cdb998'],desc:'The main beach of the Cinque Terre, at Fegina below the village of Monterosso. It mixes paid lidos with a small free area by the train station, and the sand has pebbles at the water line.',fac:'Paid lidos with showers, cabins and cafes; fewer facilities on the free sand',park:'Reached on foot from the train station, so a car is not needed',tip:'Bring water shoes for the pebbles. Lido sunbeds are often cash only, and a shallow area near the Giant statue suits young children.'},
{id:'sisine',name:'Cala Sisine',loc:'Baunei, Gulf of Orosei, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Remote Gulf of Orosei cove at the mouth of a canyon',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:40.1797,lng:9.6338,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e6d9b8'],desc:'A remote cove in the Gulf of Orosei, where a green canyon opens onto pale sand and shingle. It is reached by boat or on foot, which keeps it quieter than the big resort beaches.',fac:'A small seasonal bar; otherwise no facilities, so bring water and shade',park:'No parking at the beach; boats run from Cala Gonone and Santa Maria Navarrese, or you can walk from the Golgo plateau parking areas',tip:'Wear sturdy shoes and carry water and an umbrella. Dirt roads on the Golgo side can be hard after rain, so check conditions locally before driving.'},
{id:'calobra',name:'Sa Calobra',loc:'Escorca, Serra de Tramuntana, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble cove at the foot of a famous mountain road',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.8508,lng:2.7995,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#b7a58b'],desc:'A small pebble cove at the end of a winding mountain road in the Serra de Tramuntana. The Torrent de Pareis gorge opens onto the shore nearby, and the water is clear and cool.',fac:'Cafes and restaurants by the port; little else on the beach itself',park:'A paid car park at the port fills quickly in summer; boats also run from Port de Soller',tip:'Arrive early or late to avoid coach traffic, and wear water shoes for the pebbles. Check current car park prices before you go.'},
{id:'kolymbithres',name:'Kolymbithres Beach',loc:'Naoussa, Paros, Cyclades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sculpted granite rocks around small sandy coves',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.1268,lng:25.2352,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e8dcc0'],desc:'A beach near Naoussa on Paros, known for its smooth, sculpted rock formations that separate small sandy coves. The water is shallow and calm, which suits families.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, beach clubs, tavernas nearby, water sports',park:'Free parking nearby, but spaces are limited; a bus or water taxi runs from Naoussa',tip:'Arrive early in summer when the main section is busiest, or try one of the quieter beaches nearby.'},
{id:'burriana',name:'Playa Burriana',loc:'Nerja, Costa del Sol, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Nerja beach lined with chiringuitos',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:36.75,lng:-3.8674,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d8c7a0'],desc:'The most popular beach in Nerja, about 800 m long and backed by beach bars and restaurants. It has fine dark sand and shallow water, with mountains behind.',fac:'Sunbed and parasol hire, chiringuitos and restaurants, lifeguards and showers in season',park:'Pay and free parking nearby; spaces fill early in summer, so arrive before 10 am',tip:'Arrive before 10 am in July and August, and try a paella at one of the chiringuitos.'},
{id:'agulla',name:'Cala Agulla',loc:'Capdepera, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sandy bay backed by pine forest',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.7179,lng:3.4595,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A wide sandy bay on the north-east coast of Mallorca, backed by pine forest and dunes. The sea is clear and shallow, and the bay is roughly 500 to 800 m long.',fac:'Sunbed and umbrella rental, beach bars and basic services',park:'Parking has been restricted recently, so check current options and expect to walk or use local transport',tip:'Go early in high season, and check the latest parking situation before you drive.'},
{id:'mylopotas',name:'Mylopotas Beach',loc:'Mylopotas, Ios, Cyclades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Lively golden bay with beach bars on Ios',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:36.7125,lng:25.2955,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e8d3a0'],desc:'A wide horseshoe bay of golden sand, about 2 km from Chora on Ios. It is the island\'s busiest beach, with beach bars and tavernas along the shore and hills behind.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, beach bars, tavernas, water sports and shops nearby',park:'No dedicated public parking was found; a bus runs from Chora every 15 to 20 minutes in peak season, or you can walk',tip:'The bars are concentrated at the southern end, so walk north for a quieter stretch. Book sunbeds ahead in July and August.'},
{id:'canyamel',name:'Canyamel Beach',loc:'Canyamel, Capdepera, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Small sandy cove in a green valley',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.6569,lng:3.4412,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A small sandy beach of roughly 300 m at the mouth of a green valley on the east coast of Mallorca. A freshwater stream sometimes forms a shallow pool behind the sand.',fac:'Sunbed and parasol hire, toilets and showers, nearby cafes and restaurants',park:'No beach-specific parking details were found; arrive early in summer to find a space',tip:'Arrive early in July and August, and check with the resort about parking before you drive.'},
{id:'levanto',name:'Levanto Beach',loc:'Levanto, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sand-and-pebble beach near the Cinque Terre',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:44.1695,lng:9.6075,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d8c8a4'],desc:'A wide bay of sand and pebbles in Levanto, a short train ride from the Cinque Terre. It has both free stretches and paid lidos, and a seafront promenade behind.',fac:'Paid lidos, free sections, surf school, cafes and restaurants',park:'Paid car parks in town; the lot above the beach has a reduced hourly rate and is not free',tip:'The beach is a calmer base than the Cinque Terre villages, and a cycle path runs along the old railway to Bonassola and Framura.'},
{id:'galdana',name:'Cala Galdana',loc:'Cala Galdana, Ferreries, Menorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Half-moon cove with calm turquoise water',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.9389,lng:3.9624,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e2bc'],desc:'A half-crescent cove of white sand and calm, shallow water on the south coast of Menorca, ringed by pine-covered cliffs. It is a popular family beach with a small resort behind it.',fac:'Sunbed and umbrella hire, toilets, lifeguards, beach bars, restaurants, paddle boats and water sports',park:'Free car parks within about 5 to 15 minutes on foot, including Cala Mitjana; a bus stop is close to the beach',tip:'Arrive early since spaces fill by midday, and walk the coast path to quieter coves if the main beach is crowded.'},
{id:'baule',name:'La Baule Beach',loc:'La Baule-Escoublac, Pays de la Loire',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'One of Europe\'s longest sandy bays',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:47.28,lng:-2.39,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#ead9a8'],desc:'A sweeping semicircular bay of fine pale sand, about 9 km long between Pornichet and Le Pouliguen. It is backed by a seafront promenade and one of the longest beaches in Europe.',fac:'Beach clubs, striped beach huts, promenade cafes, lifeguards in summer, cycle path along the bay',park:'Parking nearby is not described in sources I found; reserved accessible spaces are available',tip:'The bay is long enough to find space even in summer. Lifeguards are on duty in July and August, so check the flags and swim within the supervised area.'},
{id:'camogli',name:'Camogli Beach',loc:'Camogli, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach below a pastel fishing village',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:44.3507,lng:9.1513,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#b9a98c'],desc:'A curved pebble beach beneath the tall pastel houses and basilica of Camogli. Free stretches sit beside paid lidos, and the village harbour is a short walk away.',fac:'Paid lidos with sunbeds and umbrellas, a free stretch with basic showers, cafes and restaurants in the village',park:'Parking is tight and many spaces are reserved for residents; the train to Camogli-San Fruttuoso station is the easier option',tip:'Bring water shoes for the small pebbles. Lidos cost about 40 EUR a day for two sunbeds and an umbrella in spring, so check prices first.'},
{id:'bidart',name:'Bidart Beach',loc:'Bidart, Basque Coast, Nouvelle-Aquitaine',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Central Bidart beach on the Basque coast',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.4374,lng:-1.5961,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d9c9a3'],desc:'The central beach of Bidart, one of the village beaches on the Basque coast between Biarritz and Saint-Jean-de-Luz. It faces the open Atlantic and attracts surfers as well as families.',fac:'Lifeguards in peak season; other facilities not confirmed',park:'Parking was not confirmed for this beach; the nearby Uhabia beach has free car parks',tip:'Check the swell and lifeguard flags before swimming, as the Atlantic surf can be strong.'},
{id:'valdevaqueros',name:'Playa de Valdevaqueros',loc:'Tarifa, Cadiz, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long wild beach with a giant dune and kitesurfing',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:36.0631,lng:-5.6795,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A long open beach west of Tarifa, backed by the large Punta Paloma dune. It is one of the best known kitesurfing and windsurfing spots in Europe, with plenty of room to swim and walk.',fac:'Several chiringuitos, kite, wind and paddle surf schools',park:'Small paid car parks along the access road; one guide reports about 5 EUR for the day, so check the current fee',tip:'The kite area is at the southern end and the northern end suits swimmers and windsurfers. Watch for rocks at the south end and strong wind.'},
{id:'costarei',name:'Costa Rei',loc:'Costa Rei, Castiadas, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long white-sand beach in south-east Sardinia',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:39.2417,lng:9.5694,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#efe3c0'],desc:'A long beach of fine white sand and clear shallow water on the south-east coast of Sardinia. Sources put it at 8 to 12 km, with free stretches alternating with paid beach establishments.',fac:'Beach establishments with equipment hire, restaurants and parking',park:'Parking is available near the beach establishments; details vary by stretch',tip:'Walk along the shore until you find a quieter stretch of free beach.'},
{id:'santelm',name:'Sant Elm Beach',loc:'Sant Elm, Andratx, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Small sandy bay facing Sa Dragonera island',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:39.5755,lng:2.3568,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d6aa'],desc:'A small sandy bay in the village of Sant Elm at the south-west tip of Mallorca, with the island of Sa Dragonera offshore. Boats to the nature park leave from the nearby port.',fac:'Seasonal sunbeds and parasols reported; cafes and restaurants in the village',park:'A guarded paid car park sits at the village entrance; free parking is further away',tip:'Sunbed rental has been uncertain in recent years, so bring your own shade. Take a boat trip to Sa Dragonera from the port.'},
{id:'tamariu',name:'Tamariu Beach',loc:'Tamariu, Palafrugell, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Small golden-sand cove on the Costa Brava',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:41.9176,lng:3.2074,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e2cf9e'],desc:'A small golden-sand bay of roughly 180 m in the village of Tamariu, sheltered by pine-covered headlands on the Costa Brava. Fishing boats sit on the sand and a row of cafes and restaurants lines the seafront.',fac:'Showers and toilets, a lifeguard in summer, bars and restaurants on the seafront',park:'Blue-zone street parking and staffed paid car parks; spaces are scarce in summer',tip:'Arrive early in July and August to find parking, and bring your own shade as sunbed hire was not confirmed.'},
{id:'gordios',name:'Agios Gordios Beach',loc:'Agios Gordios, Corfu, Ionian Islands',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Blue Flag beach beneath steep green cliffs',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.5461,lng:19.8498,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e9d6a4'],desc:'A Blue Flag beach of about 1 km on the west coast of Corfu, backed by steep green cliffs and a rock offshore. The south end is sandy and the north end gets pebblier.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas for hire, tavernas, pedal boats and canoes',park:'Parking is scarce in July and August; there is a large municipal car park a little above the village',tip:'Go on a weekday morning for fewer crowds, as weekend afternoons are the busiest.'},
{id:'alimini',name:'Alimini Beach',loc:'Alimini, Otranto, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy Adriatic beach with clear shallow water',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:40.2012,lng:18.4594,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e2bc'],desc:'A stretch of fine sand and clear, gently sloping water on the Salento coast near Otranto, backed by pine woods and dunes. Free stretches sit between beach bars and resort beaches.',fac:'Beach bars with sunbeds, resort beaches, restaurants nearby',park:'Parking is limited and can be hard to find at busy times; some free public parking was reported',tip:'Arrive early in summer, and check the beach bar prices first as an older review reported about 10 EUR for two loungers and an umbrella.'},
{id:'marinagrande',name:'Marina Grande Beach',loc:'Marina Grande, Sorrento, Campania',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Small beach by a colourful fishing harbour',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:40.6275,lng:14.3656,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#bfae92'],desc:'A small public beach of volcanic sand and rocks beside the old fishing harbour of Marina Grande in Sorrento, with colourful houses and restaurants around it.',fac:'Seafront restaurants and cafes; the paid sunbed concessions are at nearby Marina Piccola',park:'Parking was not confirmed; the walk down from the town is steep and buses or taxis help',tip:'Bring a mat or camping chair as the shore is rocky. Marina Piccola has the paid sunbeds and a lift down from the town.'},
{id:'valelobo',name:'Praia do Vale do Lobo',loc:'Vale do Lobo, Loule, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Resort beach below red Algarve cliffs',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.0487,lng:-8.066,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#ecd9a8'],desc:'A wide sandy beach below the ochre cliffs of the Vale do Lobo resort on the central Algarve. The Praca area above the beach holds restaurants and bars, and a Blue Flag has been reported.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, beach bars and restaurants, a massage station',park:'Plenty of paid parking; bring coins for the meter',tip:'The first rows of sunbeds are reserved for resort guests. One visitor paid about 40 EUR for a sunbed and umbrella, so check the price first.'},
{id:'kavourotrypes',name:'Kavourotrypes Beach',loc:'Sithonia, Halkidiki',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'rocky',tag:'Turquoise rock-pool coves on Sithonia',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:40.1265,lng:23.9703,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#f3d9a4'],desc:'A string of small coves on the east coast of Sithonia, also known as Orange Beach. White rocks frame clear turquoise water, with small patches of sand between the outcrops.',fac:'A few sunbeds and a small beach bar near the main cove; a toilet near the car park; no showers or changing cabins',park:'Free parking under the trees above the beach; it fills quickly in July and August',tip:'The walk from the car park to the beach takes 3 to 4 minutes along a path through the woods. Go before 11 am in high season, and bring your own shade for the quieter natural coves.'},
{id:'superparadise',name:'Super Paradise Beach',loc:'Plintri, Mykonos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Mykonos beach club cove below a steep hillside',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.4148,lng:25.3685,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f1d9a7'],desc:'A sandy cove on the south coast of Mykonos, known for its beach clubs and lively atmosphere. The beach sits below a steep access road, with clear water and a mix of paid and open sand.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, beach clubs with a DJ, a restaurant, water sports and massages',park:'Free parking above the beach; the final stretch of road is steep, and valet attendants may expect a tip',tip:'Recent guides report about 25 to 40 EUR for two sunbeds with an umbrella, while some reviews report far higher prices in peak season, so check before you sit down. A local bus links Mykonos Town roughly every couple of hours.'},
{id:'agiossostis',name:'Agios Sostis Beach',loc:'Mykonos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet northern Mykonos cove away from the clubs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.4855,lng:25.3577,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e9d6a6'],desc:'A quiet sandy beach on the north coast of Mykonos, far from the busy clubs of the south. The beach is undeveloped, with no organised sunbeds and a single taverna nearby.',fac:'No sunbeds or umbrellas to rent; a taverna nearby',park:'Roadside parking on the narrow access road; arrive early',tip:'Bring your own umbrella, water and cash for the taverna, since there is little shade. A section at the far end is used by nude sunbathers.'},
{id:'kalamitsi',name:'Kalamitsi Beach',loc:'Kalamitsi, Lefkada',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Wild white-pebble coves under steep cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.7571,lng:20.6042,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e8e4da'],desc:'A string of pebble coves on the west coast of Lefkada below the village of Kalamitsi, with clear water under steep cliffs. Kavalikefta, Megali Petra and Avali lie close together along the same rough road.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas for rent at Kavalikefta with a restaurant above the beach; a snack bar at Avali; nothing at Megali Petra',park:'A small private car park at the end of the road at Kavalikefta; limited parking at Avali',tip:'The access road is steep and narrow, and cars cannot pass each other in places. Arrive early and drive slowly.'},
{id:'timoni',name:'Porto Timoni',loc:'Afionas, Corfu',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Twin bays reached by a clifftop hike',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:39.7151,lng:19.6578,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9ecd6'],desc:'Two back-to-back coves on the north-west coast of Corfu, separated by a narrow strip of land. The only way in is on foot from the village of Afionas along a rocky path.',fac:'No facilities reported on the beach; tavernas in Afionas',park:'Limited parking in Afionas fills fast in summer; one guide mentions a paid lot of about 5 EUR at the trailhead',tip:'Allow roughly 30 to 40 minutes each way on a rocky, partly steep path, wear sturdy shoes, and go early in the morning to avoid the heat and the crowds. The viewpoint above the coves is a short detour.'},
{id:'kolona',name:'Kolona Beach',loc:'Kythnos, Cyclades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Double sandbar joining Kythnos to a tiny islet',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:37.414,lng:24.3788,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f0ddb0'],desc:'A narrow strip of fine sand joining the main island of Kythnos to the islet of Agios Loukas, with water on both sides. It is widely described as the most famous beach on the island.',fac:'Limited: a beach bar or taverna on part of the beach, reported with some sunbeds; little natural shade',park:'Parking is at Fikiada, not at the beach itself; a rough dirt road runs from Chora',tip:'Bring your own shade, since there are only a couple of trees. Taxi boats run from Merichas in about 15 minutes if you would rather skip the dirt road.'},
{id:'chia',name:'Sa Colonia Beach',loc:'Chia, Domus de Maria, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandy beach beside a flamingo lagoon',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.893,lng:8.8795,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f2dcae'],desc:'A sandy beach at Chia on the south coast of Sardinia, with a coastal lagoon behind it where pink flamingos sometimes feed. The area has kiosks and small services but no large beach clubs.',fac:'Kiosks renting loungers and umbrellas, with food and drinks; toilets and changing rooms',park:'Paid parking in season, about 7 to 8 EUR a day; free out of season; about a 10 minute walk to the sand',tip:'Reviews mention a cheaper parking rate after 4 pm. The bus stop is Chia Tabacchi, followed by a short walk.'},
{id:'fiascherino',name:'Fiascherino Beach',loc:'Fiascherino, Lerici, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Small bay on the Gulf of Poets',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:44.0662,lng:9.9249,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e5d3a6'],desc:'A small cove on the Gulf of La Spezia between Lerici and Tellaro. Two beaches sit on either side of a rocky promontory, with steps leading down to the water.',fac:'Deckchairs and umbrellas on the equipped stretch, with a lifeguard in season; part of the beach is free',park:'Paid parking about 200 m away, with free parking about 500 m away',tip:'One visitor paid 25 EUR for two sunbeds and an umbrella from 2 pm, so check prices first. A beach club between Fiascherino and Lerici is reached by lift or steps.'},
{id:'puntaprosciutto',name:'Punta Prosciutto',loc:'Porto Cesareo, Salento, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Ionian sand beach with dunes and lidos',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:40.2945,lng:17.7661,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f4e3b9'],desc:'A long sandy beach on the Ionian coast of Salento, backed by dunes and part of a protected area within the Porto Cesareo marine reserve. It mixes free sand with paid lido areas.',fac:'Lidos with loungers and umbrellas, such as Samana Beach, Teranga Bay and Lido Oasis, plus bars and showers',park:'Paid, seasonal parking; bring change',tip:'Late spring and early autumn are quieter than July and August. Use the marked paths and keep off the dune vegetation.'},
{id:'calamosche',name:'Calamosche Beach',loc:'Vendicari, Noto, Sicily',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Small sandy cove inside Vendicari reserve',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:36.8243,lng:15.1056,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#efdcae'],desc:'A small sandy cove between rocky headlands inside the Vendicari nature reserve on the south-east coast of Sicily. The beach is reached on foot from the car park and has no shade.',fac:'No sunbeds and no shade; a bar and showers are reported at the car park',park:'Private car park at the reserve, about 5 EUR reported, plus a reserve entry fee',tip:'One French guide says the reserve admits about 550 visitors a day, so arrive early in summer. Bring an umbrella and water for the walk of roughly 1 km.'},
{id:'zavial',name:'Praia do Zavial',loc:'Raposeira, Vila do Bispo, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet sandy bay near Sagres',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.0463,lng:-8.8715,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#efdcae'],desc:'A broad sandy bay on the western Algarve, backed by low cliffs and a beachfront restaurant. The Atlantic water is cooler than on the central Algarve and waves can be strong.',fac:'Restaurant behind the beach, toilets, some sunbeds, lifeguards in peak season; no showers',park:'A car park near the restaurant; limited in summer',tip:'The restaurant reportedly opens only in high season and takes cash only, with an ATM nearby. Leave the N125 near Raposeira and follow the signs.'},
{id:'ingrina',name:'Praia da Ingrina',loc:'Raposeira, Vila do Bispo, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered cove with a seafood restaurant',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.0467,lng:-8.8791,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f0dcab'],desc:'A small sandy cove on the western Algarve near Raposeira, sheltered by rocks. A seafood restaurant sits by the sand with views over the bay.',fac:'Restaurant and bar, sunbeds and umbrellas for rent, toilets, lifeguards in summer',park:'A car park close to the beach',tip:'There is little natural shade, though the wind often softens the sun. Take the N125 at Raposeira.'},
{id:'salema',name:'Praia da Salema',loc:'Salema, Budens, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Fishing village beach with golden sand',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.065,lng:-8.8246,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f3dfb0'],desc:'A Blue Flag beach beside the fishing village of Salema on the western Algarve, with golden sand between low cliffs and a line of beachfront restaurants.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, restaurants and bars along the front; the quieter eastern end has no rentals',park:'Parking near the village; spaces fill up in peak season and on weekends',tip:'Walk to the eastern end for a quieter stretch without sunbed rentals. Nearby restaurants include Olhos n Agua and O Lourenco.'},
{id:'lances',name:'Playa de Los Lances',loc:'Tarifa, Cadiz, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide windy beach for kitesurfing',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:36.03,lng:-5.6241,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#f1dfb4'],desc:'A long, open sandy beach on the Strait of Gibraltar just north-west of Tarifa, known for kitesurfing and windsurfing. Africa is visible across the water on clear days.',fac:'Parking, toilets, showers and sunbeds are reported at Lances Sur, with beach bars nearby',park:'Plenty of parking for private cars; the Tarifa bus station is nearby',tip:'Strong wind can make sunbathing unpleasant, and levante is offshore, so take care when swimming. One comment says kiting is banned here in summer, from 15 June to 15 September, which I could not confirm, so check with the Tarifa council.'},
{id:'torta',name:'Cala Torta',loc:'Arta, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild sand cove with a long walk in',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.7498,lng:3.4177,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#efdcae'],desc:'A wide, undeveloped sand beach on the north-east coast of Mallorca near Arta, with golden sand and clear water. The final approach is a walk from an unpaved parking area.',fac:'No facilities and no lifeguards; a small food truck or restaurant sits before the trail starts',park:'Park on the unpaved road about 1.2 to 1.5 km away; driving closer is not allowed',tip:'The walk takes 15 to 30 minutes each way on an uneven trail, uphill on the way back. Bring water, shade and sneakers. Phone signal is poor, and northerly winds can create undercurrents.'},
{id:'calblanque',name:'Playa de Calblanque',loc:'Cartagena, Murcia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Protected park beaches with no buildings',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:37.6037,lng:-0.7302,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e6d2a3'],desc:'A string of sandy coves inside Calblanque Regional Park on the Murcia coast, with dunes and low hills and no buildings behind the beach. Car access is restricted in summer to protect the park.',fac:'No beach bar found in my sources; the Las Cobaticas visitor centre is inside the park',park:'Summer vehicle access is restricted; a free lot of about 30 spaces is reported, but it may close in high season',tip:'Check the park rules before driving in summer. A bus or shuttle may run on busy days, and the Las Cobaticas visitor centre can advise on parking and maps.'},
{id:'starabaska',name:'Stara Baska Beach',loc:'Stara Baska, Krk',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Long pebble bay at the southern tip of Krk',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:44.9526,lng:14.6903,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#dcd9cf'],desc:'A long bay at the southern tip of Krk with fine gravel and pebbles and clear water, framed by bare limestone hills. One road runs through the village.',fac:'One guide lists showers, a beach bar, restaurants, sun loungers, umbrellas and changing rooms',park:'Limited roadside parking; several beaches sit before the village entrance and are reached on foot',tip:'One guide says the main beach can only be reached by sea, while others describe road access, so check locally. Oprna cove nearby has a small bar in peak season and a steep walk of 10 to 15 minutes.'},
{id:'kupari',name:'Kupari Beach',loc:'Zupa dubrovacka, near Dubrovnik',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach below ruined Yugoslav-era hotels',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:42.6236,lng:18.1893,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#d8d3c6'],desc:'A pebble beach in Zupa dubrovacka, about 10 km south of Dubrovnik, beside the shell of a military holiday resort built for Yugoslav army officers. The hotels have been abandoned since the 1991 siege of Dubrovnik, and redevelopment work began on the site in 2025.',fac:'The old bathing facilities have been disused for years; bring your own water and shade',park:'I found no parking details; check on arrival',tip:'The site is a redevelopment zone, so check access and any fencing before you go.'},
{id:'zavala',name:'Zavala Beach',loc:'Zavala, Hvar',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble cove on Hvar south coast reached by tunnel',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.1234,lng:16.6961,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e3ddd0'],desc:'A pebble and gravel beach in the village of Zavala on the quiet south coast of Hvar. The village is reached from Pitve through a tunnel, with a signposted car park near the beach.',fac:'Konoba Zavala, Zaca Bar and Restaurant and Restaurant Davor nearby; I found no sunbed rental details',park:'A signposted car park near the beach',tip:'Zavala is on the quiet side of Hvar and known for Bogdanjusa white wine. Check locally for sunbed rental.'},
{id:'nin',name:'Nin Beach',loc:'Nin, Zadar County',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'sandy',tag:'Shallow sandy lagoon beach with pine shade',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:44.2514,lng:15.1752,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f1ddb0'],desc:'Queen Beach (Kraljicina plaza) is a sandy beach of more than 2 km on the Nin lagoon near Zadar. The water stays shallow for up to about 500 m from the shore, which suits small children. The lagoon bed is sand and mud and shifts with the weather.',fac:'Sun loungers and umbrellas for rent, and a beach bar nearby',park:'Public parking in the small pine forest; paid in summer, reported free in September',tip:'The mud of the Nin lagoon is known as peloid and is found in the shallows.'},
{id:'pakostane',name:'Pakostane Beach',loc:'Pakostane, Zadar County',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pine-shaded bay on the Zadar coast',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.9083,lng:15.5061,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e2dcc9'],desc:'A pine-shaded bay on the coast between Zadar and Sibenik, with a mix of sand, shingle and rocky terraces. Pine trees run down almost to the shore.',fac:'Sun loungers and umbrellas are reported at the Pine Beach resort; a car park among the trees',park:'A car park among the trees at the entrance; one listing says free',tip:'Sources disagree on whether the shore is mainly sand or rock, so expect a mix. Check which stretch is public.'},
{id:'piemanson',name:'Plage de Piemanson',loc:'Salin-de-Giraud, Camargue',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Camargue dune beach at the Rhone mouth',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.3398,lng:4.814,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e6d6b0'],desc:'A long, wild sandy beach on the Camargue coast near the mouth of the Rhone, with dunes and few buildings. It is known for kitesurfing and for its long-standing wild camping season.',fac:'No showers or toilets reported; a supervised swimming zone in summer',park:'A public car park open from 6:00 to 22:00, according to the Arles tourist office',tip:'Bring water, shade and food. Dogs are banned in the supervised swimming zone, and the east end near the Rhone mouth is naturist.'},
{id:'tahiti',name:'Plage de Tahiti',loc:'Ramatuelle, Var, Provence',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Northern end of Pampelonne bay',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.2442,lng:6.6661,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f2e0b6'],desc:'The northern end of the long Pampelonne bay near Ramatuelle on the French Riviera, with fine sand and a line of beach restaurants. Public access to the beach is free.',fac:'Beach restaurants and clubs such as Restaurant Tahiti Beach and Tiki Club, with paid sunbeds',park:'Paid parking in summer; Pampelonne parking is reported free before 11 am and after 5 pm in season',tip:'Sunbed prices at the Pampelonne clubs are high: one listing shows 40 to 60 EUR for a sunbed, while another shows 33 EUR for a mattress or umbrella. A boat shuttle is suggested in July as an alternative to hunting for parking.'},
{id:'palue',name:'Plage de la Palue',loc:'Crozon, Finistere, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild surf beach under Crozon cliffs',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:48.1994,lng:-4.5523,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:17,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#e8dab4'],desc:'A wild sandy beach on the west coast of the Crozon peninsula in Brittany, popular with surfers for its Atlantic waves. A car park on the dune top gives a short walk to the sand.',fac:'No lifeguards; no services reported on the beach',park:'A large car park at the top of the dune, a short walk from the beach',tip:'Swimming is reported to be prohibited because of strong currents, and no lifeguards are on duty. A large part of the beach floods at high tide. Parking rules at some Crozon car parks changed in 2021, so check with the Crozon town hall.'},
{id:'torche',name:'Pointe de la Torche',loc:'Plomeur, Finistere, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Big-wave Breton surf beach',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:47.8367,lng:-4.3544,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:17,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d9b8'],desc:'A wide sandy beach beside the Pointe de la Torche in south Finistere, one of the best-known surf spots in Brittany. The waves are often big, and the spot is open all year to experienced surfers.',fac:'A large car park, toilets, surf shops, restaurants and surf schools',park:'A large car park; the direct road to the point may be closed at busy times, with lots and a paid shuttle (about 2 EUR return) in use',tip:'Lifeguards cover the beach only in July and August, from 1.30 pm to 7.30 pm. The waves suit surfers with a good level.'},
{id:'miknaxos',name:'Mikri Vigla Beach',loc:'Mikri Vigla, Naxos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Windy Naxos beach for kite and wind sports',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.0159,lng:25.3779,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f1e2b8'],desc:'Long, pale beaches on the south-west coast of Naxos, split into two bays by a small rocky headland. The steady summer wind makes Mikri Vigla one of the island hubs for kitesurfing and windsurfing, and the water is clear and turquoise.',fac:'Surf and kite schools, a few tavernas, little or no sunbed service',park:'Free parking along the coastal road and on dirt areas behind the dunes',tip:'Mornings are calmer for swimming; the wind usually builds in the afternoon, which suits kiters but can blow sand around. Bring your own shade.'},
{id:'apella',name:'Apella Beach',loc:'Apella, Karpathos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Remote pebble cove in north Karpathos',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:35.6027,lng:27.1588,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9d2c0'],desc:'A pretty bay of white pebbles and very clear water on the east coast of Karpathos, set under green hills. It is about 20 km from Pigadia, and the last part of the trip is on a winding road that ends above the cove.',fac:'A small taverna, sunbed and umbrella sets for rent, no shops',park:'A small car park by the taverna where the road ends, then a short path down to the beach',tip:'Bring water and shoes for the pebbles. Excursion boats from Pigadia are an easy alternative to the long drive, and a public bus runs on a few days a week, so check times.'},
{id:'katergo',name:'Katergo Beach',loc:'Katergo, Folegandros',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Wild cove under cliffs, reached by boat or hike',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:36.5948,lng:24.9491,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0c4a6e','#cfc7b4'],desc:'A wild, unspoilt cove on the south-east side of Folegandros, backed by tall cliffs and with deep blue water. There are no facilities, which is a large part of its charm.',fac:'None. Bring your own water, food and shade',park:'No parking at the beach; park at Livadi or Karavostasi and walk or take the boat',tip:'Small boats leave Karavostasi in summer (about 10 minutes), or you can hike for 30 to 50 minutes from Livadi. Go early and carry water; there is almost no shade.'},
{id:'kalafatis',name:'Kalafatis Beach',loc:'Kalafatis, Mykonos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy bay with water sports on Mykonos',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.4351,lng:25.4204,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f2e4bc'],desc:'A long golden bay on the east coast of Mykonos, with a more relaxed feel than the famous party beaches. Windsurf and kitesurf schools use the bay, and a stretch at the far end stays wilder and quieter.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, several restaurants and bars, water sports schools',park:'Free street parking near the beach, plus a bus from Mykonos Town Old Port',tip:'The organised section is busy in July and August. Walk east along the sand for a quieter stretch with no services.'},
{id:'agiosioannis',name:'Agios Ioannis Beach',loc:'Agios Ioannis, Pelion',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach beside a Pelion seaside village',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:39.3886,lng:23.2514,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d8d0bc'],desc:'A long pebble beach on the Aegean side of Pelion, with forested slopes behind and calm, clear water. The village has a boardwalk lined with tavernas, so it works well for a relaxed day with good food.',fac:'Tavernas along the boardwalk, a few rooms and hotels, limited sunbed rental',park:'Free parking is hard to find in July and August; some hotels have small private lots',tip:'Arrive early in peak season for a parking space. The pebbles are sharp in places, so water shoes help.'},
{id:'lacinta',name:'La Cinta Beach',loc:'San Teodoro, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long white-sand beach by a lagoon',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:40.7952,lng:9.67,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f6efd6'],desc:'A long strip of soft white sand and shallow turquoise water just outside San Teodoro, with a lagoon behind it. It is one of the most popular beaches in north-east Sardinia and a favourite for families.',fac:'Beach clubs with sunbeds, bars, restaurants, showers and toilets',park:'Free and paid parking near the entrances; paid lots are pricey in summer',tip:'Sunbeds can cost a lot in August. Walk 10 to 15 minutes along the beach for a quieter stretch.'},
{id:'guaceto',name:'Torre Guaceto Beach',loc:'Carovigno, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Protected nature reserve with long dune beaches',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:40.7057,lng:17.783,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e9bb5','#efe2bb'],desc:'A long, flat, sandy beach inside the Torre Guaceto marine reserve on the Adriatic coast of Puglia. Dunes, Mediterranean scrub and a 16th-century watchtower give it a wild feel, and the sea is shallow and clean.',fac:'Reserve visitor services, a small bar and toilets near the entrance, no sunbed rental on most of the beach',park:'Paid parking at the reserve entrance (a few euros per day) with a shuttle to the beach, or a flat walk of about 1.4 km',tip:'Entry is controlled to protect the reserve, so go early in July and August. Bring your own shade and water.'},
{id:'praiano',name:'Marina di Praia',loc:'Praiano, Amalfi Coast',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Tiny cove tucked between cliffs on the Amalfi Coast',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:40.6107,lng:14.5338,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9cdb4'],desc:'A small pebbly cove at the bottom of a steep gorge, with a pretty old fishing hamlet, a few restaurants and a sea that is deep blue and very clear. It feels far from the busy towns on the same coast.',fac:'A few restaurants, a beach club, no large sunbed area',park:'Roadside parking on the Amalfi road above and a summer private car park; the SITA bus stops nearby',tip:'The descent is steep, with many steps back up. Visit in the morning, since the cove falls into shade early in the afternoon.'},
{id:'scilla',name:'Scilla Marina Grande',loc:'Scilla, Calabria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Town beach beneath a medieval castle',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.2528,lng:15.7115,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d6b0'],desc:'A long town beach in the old fishing town of Scilla, with the Ruffo castle rising above one end and views across to Sicily. The sand is pale and the water is clean, and the old quarter of Chianalea is a short walk away.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbed rental, restaurants and showers nearby',park:'A car park near the beach, paid in summer, plus street parking in town',tip:'Walk up to the castle terrace for the best view. Chianalea is uphill from the beach, so allow extra time.'},
{id:'positano',name:'Fornillo Beach',loc:'Positano, Amalfi Coast',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Quieter Positano beach reached by a coastal path',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:40.626,lng:14.4808,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d3c8b0'],desc:'A pebbly beach in a small bay west of Positano town, calmer and less crowded than Spiaggia Grande. Pastel houses climb the hill behind and a few seafood restaurants sit right on the beach.',fac:'Lidos with sunbeds and umbrellas, restaurants, toilets',park:'No beach parking; use the town car parks, then walk or take the sea shuttle',tip:'The walk takes about 10 minutes and includes long stairs. Sunbed prices are high, so a free spot on the pebbles is a good budget option.'},
{id:'torimbia',name:'Playa de Torimbia',loc:'Llanes, Asturias',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild cove with golden sand in Asturias',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:43.4427,lng:-4.852,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#efe0b6'],desc:'A beautiful, unspoilt cove of golden sand backed by green meadows and cliffs on the Asturian coast. Naturist use is common here, and the sea is clean but cool and can be strong in rough weather.',fac:'A seasonal bar, showers and lifeguards in summer',park:'A small free car park at the top, with roadside parking when it is full',tip:'The walk down takes 15 to 20 minutes and the climb back 20 to 25 minutes. The beach is clothes-optional, and the swell can bring strong currents.'},
{id:'lanzada',name:'Praia da Lanzada',loc:'Sanxenxo, Galicia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Atlantic beach with big waves in Galicia',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.4469,lng:-8.876,season:'July&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#f1e5c3'],desc:'One of the longest beaches in Galicia, with about 2 km of fine white sand backed by dunes. It faces the open Atlantic, so the waves are strong and the water is cold, but the scene is lively and wide.',fac:'Toilets behind the dunes, chiringuitos and restaurants nearby, lifeguards in summer',park:'Free parking close to the beach',tip:'Swim only where the lifeguards allow, since the waves and currents can be strong. The sunsets from here are excellent.'},
{id:'deia',name:'Cala Deia',loc:'Deia, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'rocky',tag:'Small pebble cove under the Tramuntana mountains',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:39.749,lng:2.6475,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0c4a6e','#cfc6b3'],desc:'A tiny pebble and rock cove at the end of a narrow valley below the village of Deia, with very clear water and a fishing-hut feel. It is popular, so it fills up quickly in summer.',fac:'Two restaurants by the cove, no sunbed rental',park:'Very limited parking on the winding road; plans for a bigger car park have been announced',tip:'Go early or late in the day. The road down is narrow, so a bus or taxi from Deia is a good alternative.'},
{id:'berria',name:'Playa de Berria',loc:'Santona, Cantabria',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long dune beach near Santona',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:43.465,lng:-3.4685,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e2bc'],desc:'A broad, golden beach of about 2 km with dunes, a nature reserve behind it and views to the Monte Buciero cliffs. At low tide the sand opens up a lot, and the water is generally calm.',fac:'Lifeguards in summer, toilets and showers, cafes nearby',park:'A large free car park, plus a bus from Santona',tip:'Best at low tide when there is more sand. The beach is exposed, so a windbreak can help on breezy days.'},
{id:'santanyi',name:'Cala Santanyi',loc:'Santanyi, Mallorca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered sandy cove with a natural arch nearby',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:39.3305,lng:3.1464,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f4e8c4'],desc:'A small sandy cove tucked between pine-covered cliffs on the south-east coast of Mallorca, with calm turquoise water. The natural arch of Es Pontas is a short coastal walk away.',fac:'Restaurants, parasol rental, toilets and showers nearby',park:'A free public car park a short walk from the beach, which fills up early',tip:'Do not leave valuables in the car, since break-ins are reported. Arrive early in July and August.'},
{id:'rafael',name:'Praia de Sao Rafael',loc:'Albufeira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden Algarve beach framed by sea stacks',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:37.0748,lng:-8.2807,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0d9a8'],desc:'A golden cove with striking rock stacks and cliffs on the Albufeira coast, with clear water and a calm feel compared to the town beaches. It has been awarded Blue Flag status in recent years.',fac:'Sunbeds on one side, a beachfront restaurant, free toilets and showers',park:'Parking is limited in summer, so arrive early or walk from nearby streets',tip:'Access is by a stairway down the cliff. Go in the morning, since the stacks cast shade later in the day.'},
{id:'evaristo',name:'Praia do Evaristo',loc:'Albufeira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Cliff-backed Algarve beach with a natural pool at low tide',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.0742,lng:-8.3028,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#eed8a6'],desc:'A long golden beach with red cliffs on the western side of Albufeira, with good swimming and a natural rock pool at low tide. Wooden boardwalks make access easy from the central car park.',fac:'Loungers and parasols, pedalos, lifeguards in summer, showers and toilets at the east end',park:'A central car park with boardwalks to the sand',tip:'The original beachfront restaurant was lost to a fire in 2023, so check what is open before relying on it for food.'},
{id:'portosanto',name:'Porto Santo Beach',loc:'Porto Santo, Madeira',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Nine kilometres of golden sand in the Atlantic',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:33.0836,lng:-16.2992,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f1dfae'],desc:'A nine-kilometre golden beach on the island of Porto Santo, with calm, shallow, clear water. It is a rare long sandy beach for this part of the Atlantic, and a Blue Flag section sits near the main town.',fac:'Sunbed rental, a restaurant, changing rooms, showers and toilets on the main section',park:'Parking near the main access points; availability is easier outside July and August',tip:'The ferry from Madeira runs daily, and the sand is also known for its mineral properties. Walk away from the town for space and quiet.'},
{id:'barbara',name:'Praia de Santa Barbara',loc:'Ribeira Grande, Azores',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Black-sand surf beach on Sao Miguel',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.8167,lng:-25.5488,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0f766e','#4b4b4b'],desc:'A long, dark volcanic sand beach on the north coast of Sao Miguel, popular with surfers. The Atlantic waves can be strong, but the setting is open and green, with mountains inland.',fac:'Lifeguards, toilets, showers, bars and a surf school',park:'Two spacious car parks near the beach',tip:'Currents here can be strong, so swim only where the flags allow. The beachfront restaurant may be closed for renovation.'},
{id:'kasjuni',name:'Kasjuni Beach',loc:'Split, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'City pebble beach under Marjan hill',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.5054,lng:16.4012,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#dcd8cc'],desc:'A pebble beach below the forested Marjan hill on the south side of Split, with clear water and a lively beach lounge. It sits about 3 km from the old town and is a favourite local escape.',fac:'Beach bar and lounge, umbrella and chair rental, toilets and showers',park:'A managed car park that fills quickly in summer; city bus 12 also runs here',tip:'Arrive early in summer. A coastal path along the Marjan peninsula links Kasjuni with other beaches.'},
{id:'svetijakov',name:'Sveti Jakov Beach',loc:'Dubrovnik, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Quiet pebble cove below Dubrovnik cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.6437,lng:18.1262,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#dcd3c2'],desc:'A small pebble and shingle cove east of Dubrovnik old town, with clear, deep blue water and wooded cliffs behind. It is calmer than the beaches nearest the walls, and the view of the coast is lovely.',fac:'A beach bar and restaurant, sunbed and umbrella rental, toilets and showers',park:'Limited parking near the church above the beach; city buses 5 and 8 run along the main road',tip:'The beach is reached by about 150 steps from the Sveti Jakov church, so it is not suitable for anyone with mobility problems. Check that the bar is open outside high season.'},
{id:'roccapina',name:'Plage de Roccapina',loc:'Sartene, Corsica',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Corsican bay beneath the Lion rock',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:41.4958,lng:8.9347,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e9bb5','#efe0b5'],desc:'A wide sandy bay in south-west Corsica, watched over by the Genoese tower and the granite Lion of Roccapina. Access is by a bumpy dirt track, and there are no services, so the beach stays quiet and wild.',fac:'No facilities. Bring food, water and shade',park:'A free dirt car park at the end of a rough track of about 2.5 km, with shade in places',tip:'The track has potholes, so drive slowly. A short, signposted walk starts from the main road if you prefer to leave the car and see the Lion rock.'},
{id:'cotebasques',name:'Plage de la Cote des Basques',loc:'Biarritz, Basque Coast',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Famous Biarritz surf beach that disappears at high tide',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.4749,lng:-1.5688,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e8d9b4'],desc:'A long sandy beach beneath tall cliffs on the south side of Biarritz, known for surfing and for its dramatic sunsets. At high tide the sand disappears, so tide times matter here.',fac:'Lifeguards in season, surf schools and cafes at the top',park:'Limited parking nearby; the town car parks are a better option than the roadside',tip:'Check the tide table before you go, since the exits vanish on a rising tide. Access is down steps from the cliff or along the beach from the old port.'},
{id:'groix',name:'Plage des Grands Sables',loc:'Groix, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Rare convex beach on a Breton island',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:47.6351,lng:-3.4208,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f1e4bd'],desc:'A long sandy beach on the east coast of the island of Groix, famous as one of the few convex beaches in Europe. The shape is created by opposing currents and slowly shifts over time, and the water is clear.',fac:'Lifeguards in July and August, a car park by the beach',park:'A car park near the beach; most visitors arrive by bike',tip:'Reach the island by ferry from Lorient (about 45 minutes), and book ahead in high season. Walking or cycling the coast path is a good way to see more.'},
{id:'omaha',name:'Omaha Beach',loc:'Saint-Laurent-sur-Mer, Normandy',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Historic D-Day beach with a long, flat shore',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:49.3706,lng:-0.8789,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:17,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e7dbb8'],desc:'A long, flat, sandy shoreline in Normandy, best known as one of the D-Day landing beaches of 1944. Memorials and the American cemetery above the beach make a visit both a quiet seaside walk and a place of reflection.',fac:'Memorials, a museum, cafes and shops in nearby villages',park:'Free or paid parking depending on the area and season; the direct path from the cemetery is closed, so drive down',tip:'Swimming is allowed, but check the tide times. Be respectful, since this is a place of remembrance.'},
{id:'gidaki',name:'Gidaki Beach',loc:'Ithaca, Ionian Islands',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble cove reached by boat or footpath',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.3858,lng:20.7299,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Challenging',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#d9e6ea'],desc:'A remote pebble cove on the east coast of Ithaca, backed by pale cliffs and clear blue water. There is no road to the sand, which keeps it quiet compared with most Ionian beaches.',fac:'A seasonal canteen or snack bar, some sunbeds in high season',park:'No parking at the beach; reach it by boat from Vathy or on a long footpath',tip:'Bring water, food and shade, and shoes you can walk in. Services are limited and vary through the season.'},
{id:'dafnoudi',name:'Dafnoudi Beach',loc:'Fiskardo area, Kefalonia',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Hidden pebble cove down a pine-shaded path',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.4717,lng:20.5484,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e2e8e5'],desc:'A small, sheltered pebble cove on the north tip of Kefalonia near Fiskardo, with calm turquoise water and a pine forest behind it. A rocky trail through the trees keeps the crowds small.',fac:'No facilities on the beach',park:'Free parking at the trailhead; roughly a 10-minute walk down the path',tip:'Wear sturdy shoes rather than flip-flops, bring water and snacks, and visit when the sea is calm. Watch for snakes on the path.'},
{id:'kalamaki',name:'Kalamaki Beach',loc:'Laganas Bay, Zakynthos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy loggerhead nesting beach',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:37.7385,lng:20.8885,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f1e2b8'],desc:'A long stretch of golden sand on Laganas Bay and part of the protected loggerhead nesting area. Wooden markers show where nests lie, and the beach is quiet in the evenings by design.',fac:'A small canteen and taverna drinks service, sunbeds in season',park:'Parking near the village streets; no authoritative figures',tip:'Follow the marine park rules: stay off marked nests, leave at sunset and keep umbrellas and sunbeds within the permitted zones.'},
{id:'mylos',name:'Mylos Beach',loc:'Agios Nikitas, Lefkada',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Wild beach below Agios Nikitas, by foot or taxi boat',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:38.7835,lng:20.608,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0369a1','#e5e0cf'],desc:'A wild, mostly pebbly beach south of Agios Nikitas, framed by steep green hills and bright blue water. A forest path or a short boat ride keeps it feeling remote.',fac:'One bar with sunbed and umbrella rental, little else',park:'No beach parking; park in Agios Nikitas and walk about 1 km',tip:'Wear sturdy shoes for the rough path and bring water. There is plenty of room if you carry your own umbrella.'},
{id:'sansone',name:'Sansone Beach',loc:'Portoferraio, Elba',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'White-pebble bay under green cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.8228,lng:10.2802,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#eef0ec'],desc:'A small bay of bright white pebbles and clear turquoise water on Elba north coast near Portoferraio. A short, steep path down through the hillside keeps it from feeling like a roadside beach.',fac:'A beach bar renting umbrellas and sunbeds',park:'Limited free roadside parking and a small paid lot; arrive early',tip:'Go early in summer, wear shoes for the pebbles, and expect little space. The path is steep and not suited to strollers or wheelchairs.'},
{id:'fetovaia',name:'Fetovaia Beach',loc:'Fetovaia, Elba',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden sandy bay on Elba south-west coast',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.7345,lng:10.1529,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e2b8'],desc:'A curved bay of golden sand and granite grains on Elba south-west coast, with calm clear water and a pine-scented hillside behind. It is one of the island most popular family beaches.',fac:'Beach clubs, bars, sunbeds and umbrellas, a car park behind the beach',park:'Small car park behind the beach with a few free spaces and paid spots; arrive early',tip:'Arrive early in July and August when it is very busy, or park at Marina di Campo and take a bus.'},
{id:'sinzias',name:'Cala Sinzias',loc:'Castiadas, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Shallow turquoise bay in south-east Sardinia',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.1964,lng:9.5627,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e9bbd','#f3e6bd'],desc:'A wide, gently shelving bay of fine pale sand and shallow turquoise water in south-east Sardinia, with granite rocks and pines on both sides. It suits families who want calm swimming close to Villasimius.',fac:'Umbrellas and sunbeds, a beach bar and a nearby resort',park:'Parking available around the resort and approach road; limited in August',tip:'Check the section you want; some parts are free and some are run by the resort.'},
{id:'orso',name:'Torre dell&#39;Orso Beach',loc:'Melendugno, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandy Salento bay beside the Two Sisters stacks',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:40.2745,lng:18.4301,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f5e8c7'],desc:'A wide crescent of pale sand and shallow turquoise water in Salento, guarded by a watchtower and the famous Two Sisters rock stacks. Clear water and gentle depths make it a favourite for families.',fac:'Lidos with sunbeds and umbrellas, free beach areas, bars and restaurants',park:'Paid and free car parks near the seafront; they fill quickly in summer',tip:'Free sections fill by about 8:30 on busy days, so come early or on a weekday.'},
{id:'budoni',name:'Budoni Beach',loc:'Budoni, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long white-sand family beach backed by dunes',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:40.7076,lng:9.6995,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f1e6c4'],desc:'A long sweep of fine white sand and clear shallow water on Sardinia north-east coast, backed by dunes and juniper. Part is free and part is equipped, which makes it easy for families.',fac:'Equipped sections with sunbeds and umbrellas, showers, bars',park:'Large paid car park, about 2&#8211;3 EUR a day reported',tip:'Check the south end for seaweed after storms, and arrive early in August.'},
{id:'catedrales',name:'Playa de las Catedrales',loc:'Ribadeo, Galicia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'rocky',tag:'Natural rock arches seen only at low tide',rating:4.8,feat:0,lat:43.5543,lng:-7.1574,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0f766e','#d8d4c4'],desc:'A Galician coast of towering cliffs carved by the Atlantic into giant arches and caves, walkable only when the tide goes out. It is one of Spain most photographed natural monuments.',fac:'Nothing on the sand; shops and bars in Ribadeo and nearby',park:'Two large free car parks, one asphalted and one gravel; they fill quickly',tip:'Book your free visit slot online in busy periods and check low tide times, since the arches are closed when the tide is in.'},
{id:'ris',name:'Playa de Ris',loc:'Noja, Cantabria',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden Cantabrian beach with a long, gentle shore',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:43.4925,lng:-3.5273,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f0e3bd'],desc:'A broad golden beach in Noja, Cantabria, with a long gentle shore, good swimming and dunes and green hills behind. Lifeguards watch the sea in summer.',fac:'Lifeguards, toilets and showers in season, bars and restaurants close by',park:'Car parks near Noja; they fill quickly in July and August',tip:'Arrive early in July and August, and check the tide, since the beach changes a lot between high and low water.'},
{id:'hort',name:'Cala d&#39;Hort',loc:'Sant Josep, Ibiza',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'rocky',tag:'Ibiza beach facing the mythic Es Vedra rock',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:38.8863,lng:1.2281,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0369a1','#e8dcc0'],desc:'A small, beautifully framed cove in south-west Ibiza where the dramatic rock of Es Vedra rises from the sea just offshore. Fish restaurants line the back of the beach and it is famous for its sunsets.',fac:'Sunbeds, daybeds, parasols, foot showers, a bar, lifeguards and fish restaurants',park:'Large unpaved car park of about 200 spaces, a 10-minute walk from the sand',tip:'Arrive before 10:00 in July and August, and stay for the sunset over Es Vedra.'},
{id:'rodiles',name:'Playa de El Puntal',loc:'Villaviciosa, Asturias',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden estuary beach facing Rodiles dunes',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.5285,lng:-5.38,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0f766e','#ecdcb4'],desc:'A small golden beach on the right bank of the Villaviciosa estuary in Asturias, with views across to the Rodiles dunes and a calm, semi-urban feel. It is easy to reach and good for gentle swimming.',fac:'Parking, showers, a rescue service in season',park:'Parking available; fills in high season',tip:'Dogs are not permitted on the beach from 1 June to 30 September.'},
{id:'bolnuevo',name:'Playa de Bolnuevo',loc:'Mazarron, Murcia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden beach beside the eroded Gredas rock formations',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.5618,lng:-1.3061,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e9d9b0'],desc:'A wide golden beach in Murcia with calm warm water, next to the Gredas de Bolnuevo, sandstone towers sculpted by wind and water. A beach that is quiet for its size.',fac:'Lifeguards and facilities in summer, bars and restaurants along the front',park:'Large open car park at the foot of the Gredas; rarely full',tip:'Stay back from the cliff edge of the Gredas, which can crumble and are not fenced.'},
{id:'foz',name:'Praia da Foz do Arelho',loc:'Foz do Arelho, Silver Coast',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Atlantic beach where the Obidos lagoon meets the sea',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:39.435,lng:-9.225,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#efdcae'],desc:'A wide sandy beach on the Silver Coast where the calm Obidos lagoon meets the open Atlantic, so you can pick between gentle lagoon water and ocean waves. Cliffs, dunes and fishing boats frame the view.',fac:'Restaurants and beach clubs on the sand, public amenities, water sports on the lagoon side',park:'Free and paid parking nearby; lots fill in peak season, but overflow areas exist',tip:'Choose the lagoon side for small children and the ocean side for waves, and arrive early in July and August.'},
{id:'irmaos',name:'Praia dos Tres Irmaos',loc:'Alvor, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandstone arches and caves at low tide',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:37.1197,lng:-8.5813,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#efd9a7'],desc:'A sandy beach in Alvor, in the western Algarve, with golden sandstone cliffs and rock stacks that form little arches and caves at low tide. The high viewpoint above is as popular as the sand.',fac:'Sunbed hire, bars and restaurants nearby, lifeguards and toilets in season',park:'Parking nearby; fills quickly in peak season',tip:'Come at low tide to explore the caves, and be ready for a good number of steps down and back up.'},
{id:'pessegueiro',name:'Praia da Ilha do Pessegueiro',loc:'Porto Covo, Alentejo',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Beach facing a fort-topped island',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.8324,lng:-8.7927,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0f766e','#ead8a8'],desc:'A sheltered sandy beach on the Alentejo coast looking out at Pessegueiro Island and its small fort. The cliffs and wild coast around it are part of the Southwest Alentejo and Vicentine Coast Natural Park.',fac:'Restaurants including A Ilha, toilets and showers',park:'Large car park for about 130 vehicles with a paved access road',tip:'Check ocean conditions before swimming; this coast can have strong waves.'},
{id:'zambujeira',name:'Praia da Zambujeira do Mar',loc:'Odemira, Alentejo',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Cliff-backed Alentejo beach with a surf break',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.5231,lng:-8.7878,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#e5d6ad'],desc:'A pretty cove in the Alentejo with a golden beach, dark cliffs and a lively little village on top. The Atlantic waves attract surfers, and the sea is cooler than in the Algarve.',fac:'Lifeguards in season, cafes and restaurants in the village',park:'About 20 spaces at the beach, plus more in town',tip:'Free-campers gather nearby; use Camping Zambujeira for legal motorhome stays.'},
{id:'brela',name:'Punta Rata Beach',loc:'Brela, Makarska Riviera',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach with pines on the Makarska Riviera',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:43.3709,lng:16.9227,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e7e5d8'],desc:'A long arc of small white pebbles under pine trees in Brela, with clear turquoise water and a rock off the shore. It is regularly named among the best beaches in Croatia.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, beach bars, free showers in the village',park:'Paid beach car park; cheaper options at nearby hotels and the village',tip:'Arrive early in July and August, when it gets very crowded, and bring water shoes if you prefer.'},
{id:'makarska',name:'Makarska Beach',loc:'Makarska, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Town beach under the Biokovo mountains',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.315,lng:16.9939,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#e9e4d4'],desc:'The long pebble and sand town beach of Makarska, with the dramatic Biokovo mountain wall behind it and a Mediterranean promenade along the back. Pine shade, water sports and cafes make it easy to spend a whole day.',fac:'Sunbeds, water sports, lockers, restaurants and cafes',park:'City paid parking; hotels may charge separately',tip:'Visit early on busy days, and check water quality and cleanliness, which some visitors flag in peak season.'},
{id:'zaton',name:'Zaton Beach',loc:'Zaton, near Nin and Zadar',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy-pebble beach near Nin',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:44.2308,lng:15.1641,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#eadfc2'],desc:'A long, shallow beach between Zadar and Nin on the Adriatic, mostly sand with pebbles in places. A flat shoreline and warm water make it popular with families.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, bars, a holiday resort',park:'Free parking at the resort; paid options elsewhere',tip:'Take water shoes for pebbly stretches and check prices before renting sunbeds.'},
{id:'lacanau',name:'Lacanau Ocean Beach',loc:'Lacanau, Gironde',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Big Atlantic surf beach on the Silver Coast',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:44.9781,lng:-1.2048,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#efe0b8'],desc:'A broad sandy Atlantic beach backed by dunes and pines, with strong waves that have made Lacanau one of France best-known surf spots. The central beach is lively, and the southern sections are quieter.',fac:'Lifeguards May&#8211;September on the south side, surf schools, cafes, a motorhome area',park:'Paid parking in the centre; a large car park to the south',tip:'Beware of rip currents and baines; swim only in supervised areas.'},
{id:'hossegor',name:'Hossegor Lake Beach',loc:'Hossegor, Landes',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Calm lake beach in the pines',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.6645,lng:-1.4313,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0f766e','#e8d9b0'],desc:'A calm sandy beach on the lake of Hossegor, ringed by pines and villas, offering a gentler alternative to the surf on the nearby ocean beaches. It has lifeguards in summer and is good for small children.',fac:'A bar, restaurant, toilets, showers, children play area',park:'Free car park at the entrance',tip:'Lake tides can make swimming impossible at low water, so check conditions.'},
{id:'argent',name:'Plage d&#39;Argent',loc:'Porquerolles, Var',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Silvery-sand beach on a car-free island',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:42.9985,lng:6.215,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f3ead0'],desc:'A long, silvery-white beach on Porquerolles, the largest of the Iles d&#8217;Hyeres, within a national park and without cars. Pine forest and warm clear water make it feel like the tropics.',fac:'A bar-restaurant, public toilets and a lifeguard post in season',park:'No cars on the island; reach by ferry from La Tour Fondue and cycle or walk',tip:'Take the ferry early, rent a bike in the village and bring water and sun cover.'},
{id:'cap',name:'Cap Ferret Ocean Beach',loc:'Lege-Cap-Ferret, Gironde',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Atlantic dunes at the tip of the Arcachon Bay',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:44.6863,lng:-1.2353,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Moderate',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#ecdcb0'],desc:'Wild Atlantic beaches and high dunes at the tip of the Cap Ferret peninsula, facing the Banc d&#8217;Arguin. Swimming is best at the supervised beaches, since waves and rips are strong.',fac:'Lifeguards at supervised beaches in summer, cafes in the village',park:'Parking just before the dunes; keep the access path clear',tip:'Swim only at supervised beaches such as L&#39;Horizon, Truc Vert or Grand Crohot; rips are strong on the open ocean side.'},
{id:'paradisemyk',name:'Paradise Beach',loc:'Mykonos, Cyclades',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Famous party beach on the south coast of Mykonos',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.4101,lng:25.3557,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f1e2b5'],desc:'A long sandy bay on the south coast of Mykonos, known for its beach clubs and lively atmosphere from morning to night. The water is clear and the sand is golden, with bars and water sports along the shore.',fac:'Beach clubs, bars, sunbeds, water sports, toilets and showers',park:'Limited parking near the beach that fills early in high season',tip:'Expect loud music and crowds in July and August; go early in the morning for a calmer swim.'},
{id:'quinn',name:'Anthony Quinn Bay',loc:'Rhodes, Dodecanese',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'rocky',tag:'Clear turquoise cove near Faliraki on Rhodes',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:36.3224,lng:28.2102,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#d9ddd0'],desc:'A small, sheltered bay of clear turquoise water enclosed by pine-covered rocks near Faliraki on Rhodes. It is named after the actor Anthony Quinn and is popular for swimming and snorkelling.',fac:'Sunbeds and umbrellas, a snack bar and tavernas nearby',park:'A small car park above the bay; spaces are limited in summer',tip:'The rocky seabed is good for snorkelling, and water shoes help when getting in.'},
{id:'tsilivi',name:'Tsilivi Beach',loc:'Zakynthos, Ionian Islands',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long family beach with water sports near Zakynthos Town',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:37.8156,lng:20.8719,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcae'],desc:'A long sandy beach north of Zakynthos Town with gently shelving, warm water and a lively strip of beach bars and tavernas. It offers a wide choice of water sports and suits families.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, tavernas, water sports and toilets',park:'Roadside parking and small car parks along the beach road',tip:'Mornings are calmer; afternoon wind can make the water choppy.'},
{id:'falasarna',name:'Falasarna Beach',loc:'Chania, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sandy beach with turquoise water in west Crete',rating:4.7,feat:0,lat:35.5022,lng:23.5797,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f5e6c0'],desc:'A broad golden beach on the far west coast of Crete, with clear turquoise water and views toward the Gramvousa peninsula. It is known for its sunsets and has room for everyone even in summer.',fac:'Sunbeds, umbrellas, tavernas, toilets and showers',park:'Free parking near the beach and along the access road',tip:'Wind and waves can pick up in the afternoon; stay for the sunset.'},
{id:'cipolla',name:'Cala Cipolla',loc:'Chia, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet cove near Chia with calm turquoise water',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.8935,lng:8.8702,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#14b8a6','#efe3bb'],desc:'A pretty bay on the south coast of Sardinia near Chia, with soft sand, clear water and a rocky headland. It is quieter than the better-known Chia beaches and feels wild and open.',fac:'Few facilities, usually a seasonal kiosk',park:'Free parking near the beach; spaces are limited',tip:'Bring your own shade and water, and arrive early in July and August.'},
{id:'baiaturchi',name:'Baia dei Turchi',loc:'Otranto, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild white-sand bay near Otranto in Salento',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:40.1952,lng:18.463,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#0e7490','#f0e6c4'],desc:'A natural bay in Salento, a few kilometres north of Otranto, with fine pale sand, pines and clear shallow water. It lies in a protected area and is one of the more natural beaches on this coast.',fac:'Limited facilities in the protected area; seasonal services nearby',park:'Parking areas near the pine wood, often paid in summer',tip:'Respect the dunes and protected area, and carry out all litter.'},
{id:'gaeta',name:'Spiaggia di Serapo',loc:'Gaeta, Lazio',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long family beach beneath Monte Orlando',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:41.2101,lng:13.5673,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#38bdf8','#efdfae'],desc:'A broad crescent of fine sand beside the old town of Gaeta, backed by a promenade and Monte Orlando. The water is shallow near the shore, and the beach has plenty of lidos.',fac:'Lidos with sunbeds, bars, restaurants, toilets and showers',park:'Street parking and paid car parks near the promenade',tip:'Free beach areas exist between the lidos, but arrive early in August.'},
{id:'camaiore',name:'Lido di Camaiore',loc:'Versilia, Tuscany',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Versilia beach with a pier and a long sandy shore',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.8933,lng:10.2287,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#3b82f6','#e9d8a6'],desc:'A long sandy stretch on the Tuscan Versilia coast, lined with bathing establishments and a short pier. Pine woods and the Apuan Alps frame the beach, and the area suits families.',fac:'Bathing establishments with sunbeds, bars, restaurants and showers',park:'Paid street parking and car parks near the promenade',tip:'Most of the shore is rented to bathing clubs, so book early in summer or use the public sections.'},
{id:'rimini',name:'Spiaggia di Rimini',loc:'Rimini, Emilia-Romagna',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Adriatic sand beach with a lively promenade',rating:4,feat:0,lat:44.0572,lng:12.5775,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#f59e0b','#f3e5b8'],desc:'A very wide sandy beach on the Adriatic coast, backed by a long promenade and a large number of bathing establishments. The water is shallow and warm, which makes it popular with families and young groups.',fac:'Bathing establishments with sunbeds, bars, restaurants, showers and toilets',park:'Paid car parks and street parking in the resort',tip:'Free sections between the bathing clubs are crowded; early morning is quieter.'},
{id:'benirras',name:'Cala Benirras',loc:'Sant Joan, Ibiza',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Sunset drumming cove on the north coast of Ibiza',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.0894,lng:1.4539,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0d9488','#e2d3a2'],desc:'A sheltered cove on the north coast of Ibiza with a small beach of sand and pebbles, framed by pine-covered hills and the Cap Bernat rock stack. It is known for informal drumming at sunset on Sundays.',fac:'Beach bars and restaurants, sunbeds in season',park:'Small roadside and paid parking near the cove; it fills early',tip:'Sunday sunset drumming draws large crowds, so arrive hours early.'},
{id:'benidorm',name:'Playa de Levante',loc:'Benidorm, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide city beach beneath the Benidorm skyline',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:38.5341,lng:-0.1113,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#38bdf8','#f0dfb0'],desc:'The main sandy beach of Benidorm, curving along the east side of the old town beneath a high-rise skyline. It is wide, well maintained and equipped with showers, lifeguards and a long promenade.',fac:'Sunbeds, bars, restaurants, showers, toilets, lifeguards and water sports',park:'Paid underground and street parking in the city',tip:'Very busy in July and August; the shoulder months are pleasant and quieter.'},
{id:'gijon',name:'Playa de San Lorenzo',loc:'Gijon, Asturias',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Urban surf beach on the Asturian coast',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.5427,lng:-5.659,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2563eb','#e6d9b0'],desc:'A long, curved city beach in Gijon on the Asturian coast, backed by a promenade and the old fishermen quarter. The tide changes the beach greatly, and it is popular for surf lessons and sunset walks.',fac:'Beach bars, showers, lifeguards in season and surf schools',park:'Paid street and underground parking in the city',tip:'The sea is cold and the tide moves a long way, so check the flags and the tide table.'},
{id:'malvarrosa',name:'Playa de la Malvarrosa',loc:'Valencia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Valencia main city beach with paella restaurants',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:39.4794,lng:-0.3237,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f2e3b5'],desc:'The best-known city beach of Valencia, a wide stretch of fine sand backed by a palm-lined promenade. It is known for the paella restaurants along the front and is easy to reach from the centre by tram.',fac:'Chiringuitos, restaurants, showers, toilets, lifeguards and sunbeds for rent',park:'Paid street parking nearby; limited in summer',tip:'Weekends are very busy; weekdays and the shoulder months are calmer.'},
{id:'sitges',name:'Sitges Beach',loc:'Sitges, Catalonia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden town beach with a church on the point',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:41.2359,lng:1.8144,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#38bdf8','#efdfae'],desc:'A calm golden town beach in Sitges, with the baroque church of Sant Bartomeu and Santa Tecla on the headland. It is close to the old town and has showers, lifeguards in season and plenty of cafes nearby.',fac:'Bars, restaurants, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid car parks in town; limited near the beach',tip:'Sitges is very busy on summer weekends; trains from Barcelona take about 40 minutes.'},
{id:'ofir',name:'Praia de Ofir',loc:'Esposende, Minho',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach with dunes in northern Portugal',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:41.5185,lng:-8.7878,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2563eb','#e9d7a8'],desc:'A long Atlantic beach in the Esposende area of northern Portugal, backed by dunes and pine woods. The surf is strong, and the area is known for windsurfing and kitesurfing and its relaxed pace.',fac:'Beach bars, restaurants, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking near the beach; limited in peak season',tip:'The sea is cold with strong currents, so swim only where lifeguards are on duty.'},
{id:'pescadores',name:'Praia dos Pescadores',loc:'Albufeira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Albufeira old-town beach beside the fishermen tunnel',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:37.0866,lng:-8.2501,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f3e0b0'],desc:'The central beach of Albufeira, reached through a tunnel from the old town, with golden sand and cliffs on both sides. It is popular and lively, with restaurants and bars close by.',fac:'Sunbeds, restaurants, bars, toilets, showers and lifeguards',park:'Paid parking in the old town; limited, with public car parks nearby',tip:'Very busy in July and August; go early or in the shoulder season.'},
{id:'costanova',name:'Praia da Costa Nova',loc:'Aveiro',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Striped houses and a long Atlantic beach near Aveiro',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:40.6201,lng:-8.7526,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#3b82f6','#e8d9ae'],desc:'A long Atlantic beach beside the colourful striped houses of Costa Nova near Aveiro, with wide golden sand and dunes. It has a relaxed village feel, with seafood restaurants and boardwalks.',fac:'Bars, restaurants, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking along the road behind the beach',tip:'The sea is cold and the waves are strong, so watch the flags.'},
{id:'carvoeiro',name:'Praia do Carvoeiro',loc:'Lagoa, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Small cove beach below a whitewashed Algarve village',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.096,lng:-8.472,season:'May&#8211;October',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0dca8'],desc:'A small golden beach set in a cove below the whitewashed village of Carvoeiro, with cliffs on each side. It sits in the heart of the village, so cafes, restaurants and shops are a few steps away.',fac:'Sunbeds, cafes, restaurants, showers and toilets',park:'Paid parking in the village; limited in summer',tip:'The beach is small and fills early, so arrive in the morning.'},
{id:'jagodna',name:'Jagodna Beach',loc:'Hvar, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Quiet pine-shaded cove near Hvar Town',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.1379,lng:16.6143,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Moderate',gem:1,g:['#06b6d4','#e8e0c8'],desc:'A pebble beach in a clear bay on the south coast of Hvar, east of Hvar Town, backed by pine forest. It is quieter than the town beaches, and the water is clear and sheltered.',fac:'Limited facilities; a small bar and sunbeds may operate in season',park:'Roadside parking; limited spaces',tip:'Bring water and shade, and wear water shoes on the pebbles.'},
{id:'rabac',name:'Girandella Beach',loc:'Rabac, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pine-shaded pebble beach in Rabac, Istria',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.0813,lng:14.1651,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#e5ddc8'],desc:'A pebble beach in the resort of Rabac on the east coast of Istria, lined with pines and facing the Kvarner Bay. The water is clear, and there are sunbeds and cafes along the promenade.',fac:'Sunbeds, cafes, restaurants, showers and water sports',park:'Paid parking in Rabac; limited in July and August',tip:'The pebbles are sharp in places, so water shoes help.'},
{id:'medulin',name:'Medulin Beach',loc:'Medulin, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Shallow Istrian bay with pine shade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:44.8075,lng:13.9356,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ebe0c4'],desc:'A broad bay at the southern tip of Istria with shallow water, pebble and stone beaches and pine shade. It is a family favourite, and several beaches along the coast have showers and lifeguards in season.',fac:'Sunbeds, bars, restaurants, showers and toilets',park:'Paid parking in Medulin; limited in summer',tip:'Water shoes help on rocky and pebbly parts; the shallows are good for children.'},
{id:'podgora',name:'Podgora Beach',loc:'Makarska Riviera, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Quiet pebble beach with views of Brac',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.2486,lng:17.0675,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#e8e1cd'],desc:'A long pebble beach in Podgora on the Makarska Riviera, backed by pines with views across to the island of Brac. It is quieter than Makarska and Brela, and the water is clear.',fac:'Sunbeds, cafes, restaurants, showers and water sports',park:'Paid parking in town and near the beach',tip:'A pleasant alternative to the busier beaches nearby; water shoes help on the pebbles.'},
{id:'croisette',name:'Plage de la Croisette',loc:'Cannes, French Riviera',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Palm-lined promenade and sandy beaches in Cannes',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.548,lng:7.0289,season:'May&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2563eb','#f0e0b8'],desc:'The sandy beaches along the famous Boulevard de la Croisette in Cannes, a mix of private beach clubs and free public sections. The water is calm and shallow, and the promenade is ideal for a stroll with views of the bay.',fac:'Private beach clubs, public sections, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking garages nearby; limited and costly in summer',tip:'Public sections are limited, so arrive early; the area is crowded during festivals.'},
{id:'salis',name:'Plage de la Salis',loc:'Antibes, French Riviera',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Calm town beach in Antibes',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.5705,lng:7.1287,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0ea5e9','#f0e0b8'],desc:'A sheltered sandy beach at Antibes with calm, shallow water that suits families, and views across the bay. Public sections sit alongside private beach restaurants.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach restaurants, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in Antibes; limited in summer',tip:'Public areas fill early; paid beach clubs offer sunbeds and shade.'},
{id:'dinard',name:'Dinard Beach',loc:'Dinard, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Elegant Breton beach below Belle Epoque villas',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:48.6365,lng:-2.0554,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#eadfbd'],desc:'The main beach of Dinard is a long sandy bay below Belle Epoque villas on the Emerald Coast of Brittany. The tide range is large, and the beach has striped cabins, lifeguards in season and a seafront promenade.',fac:'Beach cabins, cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid street parking in Dinard; limited in summer',tip:'Tides are large, so check the times before swimming.'},
{id:'lapad',name:'Lapad Beach',loc:'Dubrovnik, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Dubrovnik city beach on the Lapad peninsula',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:42.6561,lng:18.0761,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d6cbb4'],desc:'Lapad Beach lies in a sheltered bay on the Lapad peninsula, a short bus ride from the old town of Dubrovnik. The shore mixes fine pebbles with concrete platforms, and the water is clear and calm.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, cafes, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the Lapad promenade; the city bus is easier in summer',tip:'Take the bus from Pile Gate and swim early before the platforms fill.'},
{id:'orebic',name:'Trstenica Beach',loc:'Orebic, Peljesac',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Long family beach facing Korcula',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:42.9783,lng:17.1917,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e3d7b8'],desc:'Trstenica is a long beach of fine shingle and sand beside the town of Orebic on the Peljesac peninsula. The water is shallow and clear, with views across the channel to the island of Korcula.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid roadside parking near the beach',tip:'Winds are strong here, which suits windsurfers; swim in the calmer morning hours.'},
{id:'garoupe',name:'Plage de la Garoupe',loc:'Antibes, French Riviera',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered bay on the Antibes headland',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.5545,lng:7.1357,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#ecdcb8'],desc:'Plage de la Garoupe is a sheltered crescent of sand on the cape of Antibes, with calm clear water and a green backdrop of pines. It is a favourite Riviera beach with private clubs and a public section.',fac:'Beach clubs, restaurants, showers and a public section',park:'Paid parking on the cape road; limited in summer',tip:'Walk the coastal path up to the lighthouse for views over the bay.'},
{id:'catalans',name:'Plage des Catalans',loc:'Marseille, Provence',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Marseille city beach by the Old Port',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:43.2907,lng:5.3555,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1d6fa5','#e8dcc0'],desc:'Plage des Catalans is the closest sandy beach to the Old Port of Marseille, below the Pharo gardens. It is lively and urban, with shallow sheltered water and views toward the Frioul islands.',fac:'Showers, toilets, lifeguards in season and cafes along the promenade',park:'Paid street and underground parking nearby; the tram and bus are easier',tip:'It is busy at weekends, so go early or in the evening.'},
{id:'jesolo',name:'Jesolo Beach',loc:'Jesolo, Veneto',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Adriatic beach north of Venice',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.5058,lng:12.6506,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe0b6'],desc:'Jesolo has about fifteen kilometres of fine sand on the Adriatic coast, a short drive from Venice. The sea is shallow and warm, and the beach is lined with bathing clubs, hotels and a long promenade.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, restaurants and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront and in town',tip:'Combine it with a day trip to Venice by boat from nearby Punta Sabbioni.'},
{id:'vieste',name:'Pizzomunno Beach',loc:'Vieste, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'White sand below the Pizzomunno rock',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:41.8792,lng:16.1774,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f1e6c6'],desc:'The beach of Pizzomunno is a curve of pale sand in Vieste, dominated by a white limestone stack that gives it its name. The water is shallow and clear, and the old town of Vieste is a short walk away.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in Vieste; the lots fill quickly in July and August',tip:'Visit at sunrise when the rock glows and the beach is quiet.'},
{id:'gallipoli',name:'Spiaggia della Purita',loc:'Gallipoli, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Town beach under the old walls of Gallipoli',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:40.056,lng:17.9819,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f2e7c9'],desc:'Spiaggia della Purita is a small sandy beach just outside the old town of Gallipoli on the Ionian coast. The water is clear and shallow, and the white town walls rise right behind the sand.',fac:'Bars, restaurants, showers and sunbed hire in season',park:'Paid parking in the new town of Gallipoli; walk across the bridge',tip:'Arrive early in August, when the small beach is full by mid-morning.'},
{id:'carihuela',name:'Playa de la Carihuela',loc:'Torremolinos, Costa del Sol',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Beach with chiringuitos and the old fishermen quarter',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.6072,lng:-4.5049,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#e6d7b0'],desc:'La Carihuela is a long flat beach of dark sand in Torremolinos, backed by a promenade and the former fishermen quarter. The area is known for its fish restaurants and beach bars called chiringuitos.',fac:'Chiringuitos, sunbeds, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid street and underground parking; the train station is close',tip:'Try the fried fish at a chiringuito on the sand, and go early in August.'},
{id:'poniente',name:'Playa de Poniente',loc:'Benidorm, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide west beach below the Benidorm skyline',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.5321,lng:-0.1578,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0b84c6','#efe2bd'],desc:'Poniente is the calmer of the two big city beaches of Benidorm, with fine golden sand and a long promenade. It is backed by the high rise skyline and has shallow, clear water.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, toilets, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid underground and street parking in town',tip:'Poniente is calmer than Levante, so choose it for families.'},
{id:'armacao',name:'Praia de Armacao de Pera',loc:'Armacao de Pera, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy beach with a fishing quarter',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.1002,lng:-8.3574,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#efd9a6'],desc:'Armacao de Pera has one of the longest sandy beaches in the Algarve, stretching for several kilometres below a small resort town. The sand is soft and the water is shallow, so it suits families.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking behind the promenade; fills in August',tip:'Walk to the western end to see where the fishing boats come ashore.'},
{id:'mogren',name:'Mogren Beach',loc:'Budva, Montenegro',country:'Montenegro',cc:'ME',type:'pebble',tag:'Twin coves joined by a path next to Budva old town',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:42.2793,lng:18.8365,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d8c9aa'],desc:'Mogren is a pair of small coves just beside the old town of Budva, joined by a footpath cut into the cliffs. The beaches are made of fine pebbles and coarse sand, and the water is clear.',fac:'Sunbeds, bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in Budva; walk along the seafront from the old town',tip:'Walk the cliff path between the two coves, and go early since it gets very busy.'},
{id:'cavalaire',name:'Plage de Cavalaire',loc:'Cavalaire-sur-Mer, Var',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy family beach on the Var coast',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.1745,lng:6.535,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0aa0c8','#f0e2b8'],desc:'The main beach of Cavalaire-sur-Mer is a long arc of fine sand with a gentle slope into the water. It is backed by a seafront promenade and sits at the foot of the Maures hills.',fac:'Private beach clubs, public sections, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade and at the port',tip:'The public sections fill in July and August, so arrive early.'},
{id:'faliraki',name:'Faliraki Beach',loc:'Faliraki, Rhodes',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Lively sandy beach with water sports on the east coast',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:36.3592,lng:28.2142,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdca8'],desc:'Faliraki is a long sandy beach on the east coast of Rhodes, with shallow clear water and a wide range of water sports. The strip is lively, with hotels, bars and sunbeds along most of its length.',fac:'Sunbeds, water sports, bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Roadside and paid parking near the beach; buses from Rhodes Town',tip:'For a quieter swim, walk to the ends of the bay, away from the bars.'},
{id:'perissa',name:'Perissa Beach',loc:'Perissa, Santorini',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Black volcanic beach under Mesa Vouno',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.3523,lng:25.4723,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#3a3a3f'],desc:'Perissa is a long beach of black volcanic sand and fine pebbles on the southeast coast of Santorini, beneath the rocky ridge of Mesa Vouno. The sea is deep blue, and the black stones get very hot by midday.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking at the edge of the village; fills in summer',tip:'Bring water shoes because the dark stones heat up fast in the sun.'},
{id:'riccione',name:'Spiaggia di Riccione',loc:'Riccione, Emilia-Romagna',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Lively Adriatic resort beach with bathing clubs',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:44.001,lng:12.657,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#eedfb4'],desc:'Riccione has a wide, gently shelving beach of fine sand, organised into numbered bathing clubs along a busy promenade. The water is warm and shallow, and the resort is known for its nightlife.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, restaurants and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is close to the beach',tip:'Choose a numbered bathing club with a kids area if you travel with children.'},
{id:'alassio',name:'Spiaggia di Alassio',loc:'Alassio, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden sand on the Riviera delle Palme',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.9985,lng:8.17,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e1ba'],desc:'Alassio has a long beach of golden sand, one of the widest on the Ligurian coast, below a promenade of cafes and shops. The water is clear and calm, with the hills of the Riviera delle Palme behind.',fac:'Bathing clubs, public sections, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is a short walk away',tip:'Walk the old Budello alley behind the beach for shops and gelato.'},
{id:'termoli',name:'Spiaggia di Termoli',loc:'Termoli, Molise',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sandy town beach under the old castle',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:41.9931,lng:15.0016,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0aa0c8','#ecdcae'],desc:'Termoli has a long sandy beach on the Adriatic coast, just below its medieval old town and castle. The water is shallow, warm and clear, and it is much quieter than the beaches of Romagna.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking behind the beach',tip:'Walk the old town walls at sunset and try the local fish stew called brodetto.'},
{id:'quarteira',name:'Praia de Quarteira',loc:'Quarteira, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sandy beach in a lively Algarve resort',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:37.0653,lng:-8.0987,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e87bd','#efdcae'],desc:'Quarteira has a very long beach of golden sand and a wide promenade, with a fishing quarter at the western end. The sea is calm and the slope is gentle, which suits families and long walks.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers, toilets and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking near the promenade',tip:'Visit the fish market and the fishing boats at the western end.'},
{id:'royan',name:'Plage de la Grande Conche',loc:'Royan, Charente-Maritime',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sandy bay on the Atlantic coast',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:45.6143,lng:-1.0129,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#e9dcb6'],desc:'The Grande Conche is the main beach of Royan, a wide curve of fine sand backed by a promenade and 1950s architecture. The water is shallow, with a long tidal range and a steady Atlantic breeze.',fac:'Children club areas, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront',tip:'Check the tide table, because the sea retreats a long way at low tide.'},
{id:'deauville',name:'Plage de Deauville',loc:'Deauville, Normandy',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Famous boardwalk and striped parasols',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:49.3614,lng:0.0661,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:17,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#e8dcb8'],desc:'The beach of Deauville is a broad stretch of fine sand with a famous wooden boardwalk, Les Planches, and rows of colourful parasols. The tide is large, and the water is cool even in summer.',fac:'Beach cabins, parasols, cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the beach is a short walk',tip:'Read the names on the beach cabins, each one is named after a film star.'},
{id:'quiberon',name:'Grande Plage de Quiberon',loc:'Quiberon, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered bay on the Quiberon peninsula',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:47.4796,lng:-3.1204,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:17,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#e6dab6'],desc:'The Grande Plage of Quiberon is a sheltered curve of sand facing the bay, with calm water and a seafront lined with cafes. It is on the Quiberon peninsula, which is known for its wild coast on the other side.',fac:'Cafes, showers, sailing schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train and ferry terminal are close',tip:'Rent a bike and cycle the Cote Sauvage on the west side of the peninsula.'},
{id:'crikvenica',name:'Crikvenica Beach',loc:'Crikvenica, Kvarner',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Long promenade beach on the Kvarner Riviera',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.1732,lng:14.6916,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d9d0b4'],desc:'Crikvenica has several kilometres of pebble and shingle beach along its seafront promenade on the Kvarner coast. The water is clear and shallow, with sections of sand and concrete platforms for sunbathing.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spots further from the centre',tip:'Walk the promenade to Selce for quieter coves and a seaside path.'},
{id:'umag',name:'Umag Beach',loc:'Umag, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Old town peninsula with pebble and rock beaches',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.4324,lng:13.5224,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d3cdb4'],desc:'Umag sits on a small peninsula on the north-west coast of Istria, and its beaches are a mix of pebbles, rocks and concrete platforms. The sea is clean and calm, and the old town is a short walk away.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in Umag; the main lots fill in July and August',tip:'Wear water shoes for the rocks, and visit the town before the evening crowds arrive.'},
{id:'saranda',name:'Saranda Beach',loc:'Saranda, Albanian Riviera',country:'Albania',cc:'AL',type:'pebble',tag:'Waterfront pebble beach facing Corfu',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:39.875,lng:20.005,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0aa0c8','#d8d0b8'],desc:'Saranda is a lively port town on the Ionian coast, and its waterfront pebble beach looks across the strait to Corfu. The water is clear, and the promenade is lined with cafes and restaurants.',fac:'Sunbeds, cafes, restaurants, showers and a long promenade',park:'Free and paid parking along the promenade; walk from the centre',tip:'Combine it with a trip to the Ksamil beaches or the ruins of Butrint.'},
{id:'vlora',name:'Jonufer Beach',loc:'Vlora, Albanian Riviera',country:'Albania',cc:'AL',type:'pebble',tag:'Quiet Ionian shore north of Vlora',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:40.438,lng:19.488,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#d9d2ba'],desc:'Jonufer is a quiet stretch of coast just north of Vlora, where the Adriatic meets the Ionian Sea. The beach is a mix of sand and pebbles with clear water, and a few cafes serve fresh fish.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds in season and seafood restaurants',park:'Free roadside parking along the beach road',tip:'Visit in June or September to avoid the crowds, and bring water shoes for the pebbles.'},
{id:'primosten',name:'Primosten Beach',loc:'Primosten, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble coves around a walled island town',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.5845,lng:15.9215,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#dcd2b6'],desc:'Primosten sits on a small wooded islet joined to the mainland, with pebble beaches and clear water on both sides. The old town rises above the shore, and the coves are calm and easy to reach on foot.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and water sports in season',park:'Paid parking at the edge of the old town; walk to the beaches',tip:'Swim early, then climb to the old town church for views over the bays.'},
{id:'sirolo',name:'Spiaggia di Sirolo',loc:'Sirolo, Marche',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'White pebble beach below the Conero cliffs',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:43.517,lng:13.627,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f3eedd'],desc:'Sirolo is a hill town on the Conero Riviera, and its beaches are white pebble coves under steep green cliffs. The sea is clear and turquoise, and the nearest beach is a short walk from the town centre.',fac:'Bathing clubs, bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking at the top of the town; free shuttle in summer',tip:'Take the shuttle or walk down early, since the path back up is steep.'},
{id:'gabicce',name:'Spiaggia di Gabicce Mare',loc:'Gabicce Mare, Marche',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Family sand beach at the Marche and Romagna border',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.965,lng:12.769,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe0b8'],desc:'Gabicce Mare is a family resort at the northern end of the Marche coast, with a long beach of fine sand and warm shallow water. The cliffs of the San Bartolo park rise behind the town.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, restaurants and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the beach is a short walk',tip:'Walk up to the Monte hill for views over the coast and the old castle.'},
{id:'sabaudia',name:'Spiaggia di Sabaudia',loc:'Sabaudia, Lazio',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide dune beach below Monte Circeo',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:41.28,lng:13.03,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e9d9b2'],desc:'The beach of Sabaudia is a long, wide stretch of fine sand backed by dunes and the Circeo national park. The promontory of Monte Circeo closes the view to the south, and the sea is clear and gently shelving.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the coast road; free sections further out',tip:'Choose a free section away from the main entrance for more space.'},
{id:'lloret',name:'Platja de Lloret',loc:'Lloret de Mar, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Main bay of Lloret de Mar with coarse golden sand',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:41.698,lng:2.846,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#ebd9a8'],desc:'The main beach of Lloret de Mar is a wide bay of coarse golden sand, framed by rocky headlands and a promenade. It is lively and busy in summer, with calm water and a steep slope near the shore.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid underground parking in town; limited street parking',tip:'For a quieter swim, walk to the small coves at either end of the bay.'},
{id:'tossa',name:'Platja Gran, Tossa de Mar',loc:'Tossa de Mar, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Golden beach below the medieval Vila Vella walls',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:41.716,lng:2.934,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0dcae'],desc:'Platja Gran is the main beach of Tossa de Mar, a crescent of golden sand overlooked by the medieval walls and towers of the Vila Vella. The water is clear and the setting is among the prettiest on the Costa Brava.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, cafes, boat tours and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking at the edge of town; walk to the beach',tip:'Climb the old town walls for views of the bay, then swim from the quieter end.'},
{id:'peniscola',name:'Playa de Peniscola',loc:'Peniscola, Castellon',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach beside the castle on a rock',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:40.364,lng:0.4035,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#efe0b6'],desc:'Peniscola has a long, gently shelving beach of fine sand facing the sea, with the white castle of the Templars rising on a rocky headland beside it. The water is warm and shallow, so it suits families.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; fills early in August',tip:'Walk to the castle and old town in the evening, when the day crowds leave.'},
{id:'denia',name:'Playa de Les Marines, Denia',loc:'Denia, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long flat beach with dark sand and calm water',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:38.87,lng:0.1,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0b84c6','#e1d2ac'],desc:'Les Marines is a long, flat beach of dark sand north of Denia, with calm shallow water and very gentle slopes. The Montgo mountain stands behind, and the beach is quieter than the resorts further south.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the road behind the beach',tip:'Go in June or September for space, as August fills the main sections.'},
{id:'javea',name:'Playa del Arenal, Javea',loc:'Javea, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sand beach with views of the Montgo',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.79,lng:0.174,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb2'],desc:'Playa del Arenal is the main beach of Javea, a long crescent of fine sand with clear water and a lively promenade. The Montgo mountain and the cape of San Antonio frame the view.',fac:'Sunbeds, bars, water sports, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; limited in August',tip:'Rent a kayak to explore the sea caves along the nearby coast.'},
{id:'calpe',name:'Playa Arenal-Bol, Calpe',loc:'Calpe, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Town beach beside the Penon de Ifach rock',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.645,lng:0.056,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#ecdcb0'],desc:'Arenal-Bol is the main beach of Calpe, a wide stretch of fine sand with the great rock of Penon de Ifach rising behind it. The water is calm and clear, and the promenade is lined with cafes.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, cafes, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town and along the promenade',tip:'Climb the Penon trail early in the morning for views over the whole bay.'},
{id:'peschici',name:'Spiaggia di Peschici',loc:'Peschici, Puglia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Town beach under a whitewashed hill village',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:41.941,lng:16.014,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0aa0c8','#f1e4c2'],desc:'Peschici is a whitewashed hill village on the Gargano coast, and its beach is a long stretch of fine sand below the old town. The water is shallow and clear, and the cliffs and pine woods of the Gargano frame the bay.',fac:'Bathing clubs, bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach and at the town entrance',tip:'Walk up through the old town for views of the bay from the castle.'},
{id:'sanremo',name:'Spiaggia di Sanremo',loc:'Sanremo, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Riviera pebble beach below the Corso Imperatrice',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:43.804,lng:7.771,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7490','#d5ccb8'],desc:'Sanremo has several public beaches of pebbles and sand along its Riviera coast, with calm water and palm trees on the promenade. The old town of La Pigna and the casino are within walking distance.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is close',tip:'Combine a swim with a walk up through the old town of La Pigna.'},
{id:'maratea',name:'Spiaggia di Marina di Maratea',loc:'Maratea, Basilicata',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach on the only coast of Basilicata',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:39.995,lng:15.723,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d8d0b8'],desc:'Marina di Maratea is a small port with a pebble beach below steep green mountains, on the short Tyrrhenian coast of Basilicata. The water is very clear, and the cliffs above give shelter from the wind.',fac:'Bars, restaurants, showers and sunbed hire in season',park:'Free and paid parking along the harbour',tip:'Take a boat trip to the sea caves along the coast.'},
{id:'scalea',name:'Spiaggia di Scalea',loc:'Scalea, Calabria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Long Tyrrhenian beach on the Riviera dei Cedri',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:39.816,lng:15.79,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d6cdb4'],desc:'Scalea has a long beach of grey pebbles and sand along the Riviera dei Cedri on the northern Calabrian coast. The sea is clear and warm, and the hills behind the town rise steeply.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the seafront; paid near the clubs',tip:'Visit in June or September to avoid the August crowds.'},
{id:'marzamemi',name:'Spiaggia di Marzamemi',loc:'Marzamemi, Sicily',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet sand beach by a Sicilian fishing village',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:36.738,lng:15.121,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#06b6d4','#f0e2b6'],desc:'Marzamemi is an old tuna-fishing village on the south-east tip of Sicily, and the beaches around it are sandy and shallow, with very clear water. The village square and the old tuna works give the place a unique character.',fac:'Bars, restaurants and sunbed hire in season',park:'Free parking at the village edge; fills in August evenings',tip:'Eat fresh fish in the village square at sunset after a swim.'},
{id:'carloforte',name:'Spiaggia Guidi, Carloforte',loc:'Carloforte, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet cove on the island of San Pietro',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.153,lng:8.31,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f1e3bc'],desc:'Spiaggia Guidi is a small sandy cove on the island of San Pietro, off the south-west coast of Sardinia. The water is clear and calm, and the shore is backed by low scrub, far from the crowds of the main island.',fac:'Few facilities; bring water and shade',park:'Free roadside parking near the cove',tip:'Take the ferry from Portovesme and rent a scooter to explore the island.'},
{id:'saintemaxime',name:'Plage de Sainte-Maxime',loc:'Sainte-Maxime, Var',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Gulf of Saint-Tropez beach with a long jetty',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.307,lng:6.637,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#eddfb6'],desc:'The main beach of Sainte-Maxime is a long stretch of fine sand on the gulf of Saint-Tropez, with calm shallow water and a view across the bay to the old town of Saint-Tropez. The town is lively and easy to walk.',fac:'Beach clubs, public sections, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade and in town',tip:'Take the boat across the bay to Saint-Tropez, which avoids the road traffic.'},
{id:'menton',name:'Plage des Sablettes, Menton',loc:'Menton, French Riviera',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble beach with a colourful old town behind',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.777,lng:7.512,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1d6fa5','#d7ccb6'],desc:'Plage des Sablettes is the favourite beach of Menton, a short stretch of grey pebbles with calm water and the pastel houses of the old town rising behind. The Italian border is a short walk to the east.',fac:'Beach clubs, public sections, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is a short walk',tip:'Walk the old town stairs up to the cemetery for views over the bay.'},
{id:'sjluz',name:'Plage de Saint-Jean-de-Luz',loc:'Saint-Jean-de-Luz, Basque Coast',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered Basque bay with a curved promenade',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.387,lng:-1.67,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#ebdcb4'],desc:'Saint-Jean-de-Luz has a calm, curved bay of fine sand protected by sea walls, with a lively promenade and Basque houses behind. The water is gentle and safe for swimming, unlike the open surf beaches nearby.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is a short walk',tip:'Try a Basque cake in the old streets behind the beach after a swim.'},
{id:'bonsecours',name:'Plage du Bon-Secours, Saint-Malo',loc:'Saint-Malo, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Tidal pool beach below the old walls',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:48.656,lng:-2.0378,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0369a1','#e2d7b8'],desc:'Plage du Bon-Secours lies just below the granite walls of Saint-Malo, with a famous tidal swimming pool built on the rocks. The tides are huge here, and at low tide the beach stretches far out toward the islets.',fac:'Tidal pool, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in Saint-Malo; walk from the old town',tip:'Check the tide table and walk out to the Grand Be island at low tide.'},
{id:'figueira',name:'Praia da Figueira da Foz',loc:'Figueira da Foz, Centro',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'One of the widest beaches in Europe',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:40.15,lng:-8.87,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#f0e0b6'],desc:'The beach of Figueira da Foz is famously wide, with a long stretch of fine golden sand beside the mouth of the Mondego river. Atlantic waves roll in, and the city promenade is just behind.',fac:'Sunbeds, beach bars, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking behind the promenade',tip:'The tide goes out a long way, so keep your belongings well up the beach.'},
{id:'vagueira',name:'Praia da Vagueira',loc:'Vagueira, Centro',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet wide Atlantic beach with dunes',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:40.549,lng:-8.75,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7fb3','#eedcae'],desc:'Praia da Vagueira is a long, wide Atlantic beach of golden sand backed by dunes, near the lagoon of Aveiro. It is quieter than the better known beaches of the Algarve, with strong waves that suit surfers.',fac:'Beach bars, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking behind the dunes',tip:'Swim only in the supervised areas, as the Atlantic currents are strong.'},
{id:'durres',name:'Durres Beach',loc:'Durres, Albanian Adriatic',country:'Albania',cc:'AL',type:'sandy',tag:'Long city beach on the Adriatic coast',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:41.3,lng:19.445,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0aa0c8','#e8d9ae'],desc:'Durres has a long beach of grey sand along the Adriatic coast, close to Albania largest port and the ruins of the Roman amphitheatre. The water is warm and shallow, and the promenade is lively in summer.',fac:'Sunbeds, bars, restaurants, showers and a long promenade',park:'Free and paid parking along the seafront',tip:'Visit the Roman amphitheatre in the old town after a swim.'},
{id:'bibione',name:'Bibione Beach',loc:'Bibione, Veneto',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Adriatic beach at the Lignano border',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:45.633,lng:13.042,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe1b8'],desc:'Bibione has a wide beach of fine sand stretching along the Adriatic coast between the Tagliamento and Livenza rivers. The water is shallow and warm, and rows of umbrellas line the shore.',fac:'Sunbeds, umbrellas, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; shuttle to the beach in season',tip:'Visit the Punta Tagliamento lighthouse at the western end for a quieter walk.'},
{id:'benicassim',name:'Playa de Benicassim',loc:'Benicassim, Castellon',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long calm beach known for its music festival',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:40.051,lng:0.068,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#e6d8b0'],desc:'Benicassim has a long strip of golden sand and pebbles on the Orange Blossom Coast, backed by a promenade of old villas. The water is calm and shallow, and the coast is known for its summer music festival.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free and paid parking behind the promenade',tip:'Visit the old villas along the promenade and the Desert de les Palmes hills nearby.'},
{id:'terracina',name:'Spiaggia di Levante, Terracina',loc:'Terracina, Lazio',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach below the Monte Sant Angelo cliff',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:41.287,lng:13.262,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ebdcb2'],desc:'Terracina has a long beach of fine sand on the Lazio coast, with the rocky bulk of Monte Sant Angelo rising above the town. The water is clear and shelves gently, and the upper old town is a short drive away.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront; free sections further along',tip:'Visit the upper old town and its Roman temple after the beach, when it is cooler.'},
{id:'giardini',name:'Spiaggia di Giardini Naxos',loc:'Giardini Naxos, Sicily',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble bay below Mount Etna with a view of Taormina',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.828,lng:15.281,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#e8dcc0'],desc:'Giardini Naxos is a bay of grey pebbles and warm clear water at the foot of Taormina, with Mount Etna smoking in the distance. The seafront has bars and bathing clubs, and Isola Bella is a short drive north.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and boat trips in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront and in town',tip:'Take the bus or a short drive to Isola Bella for a quieter swim.'},
{id:'cattolica',name:'Spiaggia di Cattolica',loc:'Cattolica, Emilia-Romagna',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide family beach on the Romagna riviera',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:43.964,lng:12.738,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe0b8'],desc:'Cattolica is a classic Romagna beach resort, with a very wide strip of fine sand and warm shallow water. It suits families and has a long promenade with plenty of bars and restaurants.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, restaurants and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the beach is a short walk',tip:'Visit the Aquarium Le Navi and walk the promenade in the evening.'},
{id:'caorle',name:'Spiaggia di Caorle',loc:'Caorle, Veneto',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Fine sand beach beside a colourful fishing town',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:45.595,lng:12.887,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f0e2b8'],desc:'Caorle is an old fishing town on the Veneto coast with a long beach of fine pale sand and warm shallow water. The historic centre has coloured houses, a round-topped bell tower and a small sanctuary on the rocks.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach and the old town',tip:'Walk the old town lanes and the Scogliera Viva sea sculptures at the end of the beach.'},
{id:'finale',name:'Spiaggia di Finale Ligure',loc:'Finale Ligure, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sand and pebble beach with Ligurian cliffs behind',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:44.169,lng:8.343,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d8b4'],desc:'Finale Ligure has a long beach of sand and fine pebbles below the white limestone cliffs of the Ligurian hills. The water is clear, the town is pastel and easy to walk, and the area is also a famed rock climbing and hiking base.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; train station a short walk from the beach',tip:'Walk the old Finalborgo lanes, or hike up the coast path for views of hidden coves.'},
{id:'cadaques',name:'Platja de Cadaques',loc:'Cadaques, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Whitewashed fishing village on a quiet cove',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.288,lng:3.278,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e8e0cc'],desc:'Cadaques is a whitewashed fishing village at the far northeast of the Costa Brava, with a small pebble and sand beach on a sheltered bay. The water is clear and the village is famous as the home town of the painter Dali and an artists retreat.',fac:'Small cafes, showers, kayak and boat hire in season',park:'Paid parking at the entrance to the village; walk to the beach',tip:'Visit the nearby Cap de Creus cape for wilder coves and sunset views.'},
{id:'calella',name:'Platja de Calella de Palafrugell',loc:'Calella de Palafrugell, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Small coves below whitewashed arches',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:41.889,lng:3.181,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7fb3','#ebdcb4'],desc:'Calella de Palafrugell is a charming fishing village with small sand and pebble coves between rocks, backed by white arcades. The water is clear, and the coastal path leads to larger coves like Llafranc and Tamariu.',fac:'Cafes, showers, kayak hire and small boat trips in season',park:'Paid parking at the edge of the village; walk to the coves',tip:'Walk the coastal path to Llafranc, then swim at the quiet rocks.'},
{id:'blanes',name:'Platja de Blanes',loc:'Blanes, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long beach beside the start of the Costa Brava',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:41.674,lng:2.792,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#ecdcae'],desc:'Blanes is the southern gateway to the Costa Brava, with a long beach of coarse golden sand and a green headland behind. The old town and the Marimurtra botanical garden are close by.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; train station near the old town',tip:'Walk up to the Marimurtra garden for views over the bay.'},
{id:'salou',name:'Platja de Salou',loc:'Salou, Costa Dorada',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Calm sand bay with family resort facilities',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:41.076,lng:1.14,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#efdfb0'],desc:'Salou is a family resort on the Costa Dorada, with a long beach of fine sand and calm shallow water. The promenade has bars, restaurants and activities, and PortAventura is a short ride away.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces in side streets',tip:'Walk or cycle the coastal path to small coves on the Cap Salou side.'},
{id:'cambrils',name:'Platja del Regueral, Cambrils',loc:'Cambrils, Costa Dorada',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet sand beach by a fishing town known for seafood',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:41.067,lng:1.059,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e8d8ae'],desc:'Platja del Regueral is a long, quiet beach of sand and fine gravel near Cambrils, a fishing town known for its seafood. The sea is calm and the beach has a lower-key feel than neighbouring Salou.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the seafront',tip:'Eat seafood at the Cambrils harbour restaurants after a swim.'},
{id:'estepona',name:'Playa de la Rada, Estepona',loc:'Estepona, Costa del Sol',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide beach with palms and a flower-filled old town',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:36.424,lng:-5.145,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d4a4'],desc:'Playa de la Rada is the main beach of Estepona, a wide, gently shelving strip of dark sand and fine pebbles with a palm-lined promenade. The old town behind is known for its flower-filled streets and murals.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid underground parking near the promenade; free spaces further out',tip:'Walk the old town streets for flowerpots and murals before a late swim.'},
{id:'almunecar',name:'Playa San Cristobal, Almunecar',loc:'Almunecar, Costa Tropical',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Dark pebble beach under a castle and a green mountain',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.733,lng:-3.691,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#cfc4b4'],desc:'Playa San Cristobal is a long beach of dark pebbles and coarse sand below the Almunecar old town, with a medieval castle on the rock above. The sea is clear and steep, and the Costa Tropical is known for subtropical fruit and mild winters.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; free spaces further east',tip:'Visit the castle and Roman fish salting remains in the old town.'},
{id:'touquet',name:'Plage du Touquet',loc:'Le Touquet-Paris-Plage, Hauts-de-France',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Huge sand beach with dunes on the Opal Coast',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:50.52,lng:1.587,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#5b9bb8','#e9ddc0'],desc:'Le Touquet-Paris-Plage has a huge beach of fine sand, backed by dunes and pine woods, on the Opal Coast. The sea is cool, the tides are wide, and the town has Belle Epoque villas and sand yachting.',fac:'Beach clubs, showers, cafes, sand yachting and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces in the dunes',tip:'Walk the dunes to the north end for a quieter stretch, and check tide times first.'},
{id:'collioure',name:'Plage de Collioure',loc:'Collioure, Occitanie',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble bay under a royal castle and a bell tower',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.525,lng:3.083,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e0d6c4'],desc:'Collioure is a painters town on the Vermilion Coast, with small pebble beaches on either side of a royal castle and a bell tower on the water. The sea is clear and calm, and the harbour is full of coloured boats.',fac:'Cafes, showers, kayak and paddle hire in season',park:'Paid parking at the edge of the town; walk to the beach',tip:'Walk the painters route through the old streets, then swim at the quieter end beach.'},
{id:'lavandou',name:'Plage de Cavaliere, Le Lavandou',loc:'Le Lavandou, Var',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach facing the Porquerolles islands',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:43.136,lng:6.368,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#efdfb0'],desc:'Cavaliere is a long, wide beach of fine sand west of Le Lavandou, backed by pines and facing the Iles d Or. The water is clear and shallow, and boats leave from Le Lavandou for Porquerolles and Port-Cros.',fac:'Beach clubs, sunbeds, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the coast road; limited in August',tip:'Take a morning boat from Le Lavandou to Porquerolles and swim at the quiet beaches.'},
{id:'cabourg',name:'Plage de Cabourg',loc:'Cabourg, Normandy',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Elegant Normandy sand beach and promenade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:49.29,lng:-0.11,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#5b9bb8','#ebe0c6'],desc:'Cabourg is a belle epoque seaside town on the Normandy coast, with a very wide beach of fine sand and an iconic promenade lined with colourful cabins. The tide goes out far, and the grand hotel was a favourite of the writer Proust.',fac:'Beach cabins, cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade',tip:'Check tide times, then walk the long Promenade Marcel Proust at sunset.'},
{id:'puntaala',name:'Spiaggia di Punta Ala',loc:'Punta Ala, Tuscany',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet sand beach in a pine-wooded Maremma resort',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:42.805,lng:10.743,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7fb3','#eee0b6'],desc:'Punta Ala is a quiet resort in the Tuscan Maremma, with a wide sandy beach edged by pine woods and a small marina. The water is clear and the area is calm, with views toward the island of Elba on a clear day.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; free spaces in the pine woods',tip:'Visit the Castiglione della Pescaia old town in the evening.'},
{id:'sidari',name:'Sidari Beach',loc:'Sidari, Corfu',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sand coves and sea-carved cliffs on the north of Corfu',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.787,lng:19.701,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#efd9a8'],desc:'Sidari on the north coast of Corfu has sandy beaches and a maze of golden sandstone cliffs carved by the sea. The famous Canal d Amour is a narrow channel where visitors swim and take photos.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, water sports and showers in season',park:'Free parking at the beach edge in the village; fills in August',tip:'Go in the early morning for the best light and a calmer Canal d Amour.'},
{id:'porec',name:'Porec Beach',loc:'Porec, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'rocky',tag:'Rock and pebble swimming spots near a Roman old town',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:45.227,lng:13.594,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#d8dcc8'],desc:'Porec has stone platforms, pebbles and small concrete lidos around its old town, with clear and calm Adriatic water. The Euphrasian Basilica is a World Heritage site, and the beaches on the Brulo and Plava Laguna sides are easy to reach.',fac:'Showers, bars, sunbeds and water sports in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces further out',tip:'Swim early at the town rocks, then visit the Euphrasian Basilica mosaics.'},
{id:'caparica',name:'Praia da Costa da Caparica',loc:'Costa da Caparica, Lisbon',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic sand beach a short ride from Lisbon',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.646,lng:-9.235,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#ebdcae'],desc:'Costa da Caparica is a long stretch of wide Atlantic beach just across the river from Lisbon, with fine sand, big waves and beach bars. The nearby Fossil Cliffs and the small tourist train make it an easy day trip.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront; the bus runs from Lisbon',tip:'Take the Transpraia train to the quieter southern beaches for more space.'},
{id:'hersonissos',name:'Hersonissos Beach',loc:'Hersonissos, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Lively sand beach on the north coast of Crete',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:35.32,lng:25.385,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ebd8a6'],desc:'Hersonissos has a sandy town beach and many smaller coves along the north coast of Crete, with warm clear water and a lively promenade. Mountains rise behind, and the old town of Piskopiano is a short drive up the hill.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, bars, water sports and showers in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces along the coast road',tip:'Rent a boat to reach quiet coves, or visit the nearby Cretan villages.'},
{id:'moraira',name:'Playa de Moraira',loc:'Moraira, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Small calm cove beside a whitewashed old centre',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.689,lng:0.134,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ebdcb2'],desc:'Moraira is a small, upmarket town on the Costa Blanca with a calm sandy cove and an old fishing quarter. The water is clear and sheltered, and the cliff paths lead to small rocky coves nearby.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars and water sports in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; limited in August',tip:'Walk the cliff path north to the small coves for a quieter swim.'},
{id:'frejus',name:'Plage de Saint-Aygulf, Frejus',loc:'Saint-Aygulf, Var',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach backed by pines near the Esterel',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:43.389,lng:6.727,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e0b4'],desc:'Saint-Aygulf is a long, family-friendly sand beach near Frejus, with clear shallow water and a backdrop of pines and the red Esterel hills. It is quieter than Saint-Raphael and Frejus plage.',fac:'Beach clubs, sunbeds, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in the village; free spaces on side roads',tip:'Walk the coast path to the quieter rocky coves to the north.'},
{id:'povoa',name:'Praia da Povoa de Varzim',loc:'Povoa de Varzim, Porto',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach north of Porto with a lively promenade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:41.37,lng:-8.764,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#e8dcb4'],desc:'Povoa de Varzim has a wide, flat beach of golden sand on the Atlantic coast north of Porto, with a casino, promenade and fishing quarter behind. The sea is cool and waves are moderate, so beaches are usually staffed by lifeguards.',fac:'Beach bars, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade; metro from Porto',tip:'Take the metro from Porto and swim only where lifeguards are on duty.'},
{id:'roses',name:'Platja de Roses',loc:'Roses, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Big calm bay on the north Costa Brava',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:42.262,lng:3.181,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#ebdcae'],desc:'Roses sits on a big, sweeping bay at the top of the Costa Brava, with a long beach of fine sand and calm water. The Cap de Creus natural park and the small cove of Canyelles are a short drive away.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; free spaces further out',tip:'Drive the short distance to the Canyelles and Cap de Creus coves for clear snorkelling.'},
{id:'santapola',name:'Playa de Levante, Santa Pola',loc:'Santa Pola, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Palm-lined sand beach beside a salt-flat town',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:38.19,lng:-0.56,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcae'],desc:'Playa de Levante is a long, gently shelving beach of fine sand in Santa Pola, lined with date palms and a flat promenade. The sea is warm and shallow, and the salt lakes and flamingos of the nearby natural park are a short drive away.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; free spaces further along',tip:'Combine a swim with a visit to the Santa Pola salt flats and their flamingos.'},
{id:'gandia',name:'Playa de Gandia',loc:'Gandia, Valencia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Very wide family beach with fine golden sand',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:38.968,lng:-0.152,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#efdfb0'],desc:'Gandia has one of the widest beaches on the Valencia coast, with fine golden sand, shallow water and a long promenade. It is a lively family resort in summer and calm and local in spring and autumn.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; free spaces on side streets',tip:'Visit in June or September for space, and walk the promenade towards the marina at sunset.'},
{id:'cullera',name:'Playa San Antonio, Cullera',loc:'Cullera, Valencia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sand beach below a castle and a mountain',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:39.158,lng:-0.22,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f0e2b8'],desc:'Playa San Antonio is a wide beach of fine sand in Cullera, lined with palms and backed by apartment blocks and the hill of the castle. The water is shallow and warm, and the lighthouse hill offers views along the coast.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade; free spaces further out',tip:'Walk up to the castle and the lighthouse hill for views along the coast.'},
{id:'oropesa',name:'Platja del Morro de Gos, Oropesa',loc:'Oropesa del Mar, Castellon',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Calm bay of sand and gravel in an old resort town',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:40.092,lng:0.156,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e6d8b4'],desc:'Platja del Morro de Gos is a calm bay of sand and fine gravel in Oropesa del Mar, with clear shallow water. The Morro de Gos headland shelters it, and the old town and castle sit on the hill above.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; free spaces on the hill streets',tip:'Walk the coastal path to the small coves of the Renegado headland.'},
{id:'torrevieja',name:'Torrevieja Beach',loc:'Torrevieja, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sunbeds and thatched parasols on a warm shallow shore',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:37.978,lng:-0.675,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#eedeb0'],desc:'Torrevieja has several sand beaches within the town, with thatched parasols, sunbeds and warm shallow water. It is one of the sunniest spots on the Costa Blanca, and the pink salt lakes are close by.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; free spaces further out',tip:'Visit the pink salt lake of Torrevieja and walk the long seafront promenade.'},
{id:'guardamar',name:'Playa del Moncayo, Guardamar',loc:'Guardamar del Segura, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide beach backed by dunes and a pine forest',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:38.083,lng:-0.647,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcae'],desc:'Playa del Moncayo is a long beach of fine sand in Guardamar del Segura, backed by high dunes and a pine forest planted to hold them. The water is clear and shallow, and the setting is wilder than most Costa Blanca resorts.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking behind the dunes; fills in August',tip:'Walk the pine forest and the dune boardwalks before the beach gets busy.'},
{id:'mojacar',name:'Playa de Mojacar',loc:'Mojacar, Almeria',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach below a white hill village',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.125,lng:-1.85,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#e8d8ae'],desc:'Mojacar Playa is a long beach of sand and fine gravel along the Almeria coast, below the white hill village of Mojacar Pueblo. The sea is clear, the climate is dry and sunny, and the beach is quieter than the big resorts to the west.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the seafront road',tip:'Drive up to Mojacar Pueblo at sunset for views over the sea.'},
{id:'pineda',name:'Platja de Pineda de Mar',loc:'Pineda de Mar, Costa del Maresme',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach north of Barcelona backed by pines',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:41.62,lng:2.68,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#ecdcae'],desc:'Pineda de Mar has a long beach of coarse golden sand, with green parkland and pine trees behind and a promenade that runs for kilometres. It is easy to reach from Barcelona by train and is calm and local compared with the busy resorts.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is near the beach',tip:'Take the train from Barcelona and walk the promenade towards Calella.'},
{id:'malgrat',name:'Platja de Malgrat de Mar',loc:'Malgrat de Mar, Costa del Maresme',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Quiet sand beach by the Tordera river mouth',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:41.638,lng:2.757,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#1e88c4','#e6d8b4'],desc:'Malgrat de Mar has a long beach of coarse sand at the northern end of the Maresme coast, near the mouth of the Tordera river. Its pine campsites and open sections give it a quieter, local feel compared with nearby Blanes.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking near the river mouth; paid parking in town',tip:'Walk the river path at the Tordera mouth for birdwatching.'},
{id:'villefranche',name:'Plage des Marinieres, Villefranche',loc:'Villefranche-sur-Mer, Cote d Azur',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble bay in a deep harbour beside Nice',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:43.703,lng:7.31,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e4dcc8'],desc:'Plage des Marinieres is a small pebble beach in the deep natural harbour of Villefranche-sur-Mer, between Nice and Monaco. The water is very clear and calm, and the old town rises behind in orange and yellow houses.',fac:'Beach cafes, sunbeds, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the train station is a few minutes away',tip:'Take the train from Nice and walk the old town streets after your swim.'},
{id:'canet',name:'Plage de Canet-en-Roussillon',loc:'Canet-en-Roussillon, Occitanie',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sand beach with the Pyrenees behind',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:42.705,lng:3.035,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#f0e2b8'],desc:'Canet-en-Roussillon is a family resort on the Catalan coast, with a long wide beach of fine sand and the snowy Pyrenees on the horizon. The water is warm and shallow, and the marina and lagoon add watersport options.',fac:'Beach clubs, sunbeds, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront; free spaces further out',tip:'Visit the nearby Etang de Canet lagoon for flamingos and kitesurf.'},
{id:'roscoff',name:'Ile de Batz Beach, Roscoff',loc:'Ile de Batz, Roscoff, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'White sand coves on a car-free island in Brittany',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:48.745,lng:-4.01,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#2aa7c9','#f4efe0'],desc:'Ile de Batz is a small car-free island off Roscoff, with white sand coves, clear turquoise water and a garden of exotic plants. The ferry from Roscoff takes about fifteen minutes, and the tide can leave long sand flats at low water.',fac:'Small cafes in the village; few facilities on the beaches',park:'No cars on the island; park in Roscoff and take the ferry',tip:'Check the ferry and tide times, then walk the coast path between the sand coves.'},
{id:'pescara',name:'Spiaggia di Pescara',loc:'Pescara, Abruzzo',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Adriatic city beach with umbrella rows',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:42.462,lng:14.226,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#efdfb0'],desc:'Pescara has a wide beach of fine sand running along the city seafront, with long rows of umbrellas and sunbeds and a lively promenade. The water is shallow and warm, and the beach is very popular with Italian families in summer.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the seafront; the train station is nearby',tip:'Try the free sections at the north end for more space.'},
{id:'vasto',name:'Spiaggia di Punta Aderci, Vasto',loc:'Vasto, Abruzzo',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild sand and pebble coast in a nature reserve',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:42.163,lng:14.71,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#e8dcc0'],desc:'Punta Aderci is a protected coastal reserve near Vasto, with beaches of sand and pebbles below low cliffs and wild grass. The sea is clear, there are fewer facilities than on the main Adriatic beaches, and old fishing platforms called trabocchi stand along the coast.',fac:'Few facilities; small bar in season',park:'Free parking at the reserve entrance; fills in August',tip:'Bring water and shade, and look for the traditional trabocchi fishing platforms along the coast.'},
{id:'varazze',name:'Spiaggia di Varazze',loc:'Varazze, Liguria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long Ligurian beach under green hills',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:44.36,lng:8.577,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#e8dcbc'],desc:'Varazze is a Ligurian resort town with a long beach of sand and fine gravel, backed by green hills and a seafront promenade. The sea is clear, the town has a small harbour, and trains from Genoa and Savona stop in the centre.',fac:'Bathing clubs, free sections, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; the train station is a short walk',tip:'Walk the old town lanes and the harbour, then swim at the free sections.'},
{id:'diamante',name:'Spiaggia Grande, Diamante',loc:'Diamante, Calabria',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'pebble',tag:'Pebble bay with painted murals above the sea',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.676,lng:15.811,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e0d6c2'],desc:'Spiaggia Grande is the main beach of Diamante, a pebble and coarse sand bay on the Riviera dei Cedri. The Isola di Cirella sits offshore, the water is clear, and the old town above is covered in colourful murals.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces further from the beach',tip:'Walk the old town murals, then try the local chilli pepper specialities.'},
{id:'kardamena',name:'Kardamena Beach, Kos',loc:'Kardamena, Kos',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach with thatched parasols',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:36.765,lng:27.145,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#efd9a8'],desc:'Kardamena has a long beach of light sand on the south coast of Kos, with thatched parasols, sunbeds and warm shallow water. The village behind is lively, and boats leave for the volcanic island of Nisyros.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, bars, water sports and showers in season',park:'Free parking along the seafront; fills in August',tip:'Take a day boat to the volcanic island of Nisyros.'},
{id:'malia',name:'Malia Beach, Crete',loc:'Malia, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sand and rocky shore on the north coast of Crete',rating:4.0,feat:0,lat:35.291,lng:25.46,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ebd8a6'],desc:'Malia has a wide sandy beach on the north coast of Crete, with lifeguard stations, sunbeds and mountains behind. Parts of the shore are rocky and wild with dunes, and the Minoan palace of Malia is a short drive away.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, bars, water sports and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the beach road; fills in August',tip:'Visit the Minoan palace of Malia in the morning, then swim in the afternoon.'},
{id:'vodice',name:'Vodice Beach',loc:'Vodice, Dalmatia',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Calm pebble bay with pine shade',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.76,lng:15.78,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#d8dcc8'],desc:'Vodice has several calm pebble and rock beaches around a small harbour town in northern Dalmatia, with pine shade and shallow clear water. It is a family-friendly base and a short boat ride from the islands and Krka waterfalls.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, water sports and showers in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces near the campsites',tip:'Take a boat trip to the Kornati islands or the Krka waterfalls.'},
{id:'troia',name:'Praia Atlantica, Troia',loc:'Troia, Setubal',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Atlantic dunes on a long peninsula',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:38.47,lng:-8.89,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#2a8bb8','#f4eee0'],desc:'Troia is a long sand peninsula south of Lisbon, with wide Atlantic beaches, white dunes and clear water. It is quieter than the Algarve, the ferry from Setubal takes about fifteen minutes, and dolphins are often seen in the Sado estuary.',fac:'Beach bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking at the peninsula; ferry from Setubal',tip:'Take the ferry from Setubal and look for dolphins in the Sado estuary.'},
{id:'setubal',name:'Praia da Figueirinha, Setubal',loc:'Arrabida, Setubal',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Turquoise bay under the green Arrabida hills',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:38.485,lng:-8.97,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0891b2','#f2ecd8'],desc:'Praia da Figueirinha is a calm sand beach in the Arrabida natural park, with turquoise water and green hills behind. It is one of the most beautiful beaches near Lisbon, and the road in is limited in summer.',fac:'Beach cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Limited paid parking; a shuttle runs in peak season',tip:'Arrive early in summer, as the road to the beach is restricted at peak times.'},
{id:'espinho',name:'Praia de Espinho',loc:'Espinho, Porto',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach with a promenade south of Porto',rating:4.1,feat:0,lat:41.008,lng:-8.641,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#e8dcb4'],desc:'Espinho has a wide beach of fine sand on the Atlantic coast south of Porto, with a long promenade and beach bars. The sea is cool and waves are moderate, and surfers use the north end of the beach.',fac:'Beach bars, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade; trains from Porto',tip:'Take the train from Porto and swim only where lifeguards are on duty.'},
{id:'nafplio',name:'Arvanitia Beach, Nafplio',loc:'Nafplio, Peloponnese',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Clear pebble coves under the Palamidi fortress',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:37.56,lng:22.805,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#06b6d4','#e2dccc'],desc:'Arvanitia is a small pebble beach at the foot of the Nafplio fortress hill, reached by a path around the rocks. The water is clear and calm, and the town of Nafplio, with its Venetian old town, is a few minutes on foot.',fac:'Few facilities; small cafe nearby',park:'Paid parking in town; walk to the beach',tip:'Walk the Arvanitia promenade around the rocks at the foot of the fortress.'},
{id:'grandemotte',name:'Plage de La Grande-Motte',loc:'La Grande-Motte, Occitanie',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach with fenced dunes',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:43.56,lng:4.08,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e4bc'],desc:'La Grande-Motte is a modern seaside town with a very long beach of fine sand, backed by fenced dunes and the pyramid-shaped apartment blocks of its 1960s architecture. The water is shallow and warm, and it is a family resort in summer.',fac:'Beach clubs, sunbeds, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; large free sections',tip:'Walk the dune boardwalks and the marina, then see the pyramid buildings.'},
{id:'cavtat',name:'Cavtat Beach',loc:'Cavtat, Dubrovnik Riviera',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'rocky',tag:'Rocky coast with sea swimming south of Dubrovnik',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:42.58,lng:18.22,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#d8dcc8'],desc:'Cavtat is a small old town south of Dubrovnik, with rock platforms, small pebble beaches and a long coastal path. The sea is clear, and the Mediterranean pines give shade along the shoreline.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, kayak hire and showers in season',park:'Paid parking in town; the Dubrovnik bus stops in the centre',tip:'Walk the coastal path to the small rocky coves.'},
{id:'perivolos',name:'Perivolos Beach, Santorini',loc:'Perivolos, Santorini',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Long black sand beach lined with beach bars',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:36.356,lng:25.484,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#6b7280'],desc:'Perivolos is a long beach of dark volcanic sand and fine pebbles on the south coast of Santorini, lined with relaxed beach bars and sunbeds. The sea is deep and clear, and the beach runs on towards Perissa.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and water sports in season',park:'Free parking along the back road; busy in July and August',tip:'The black sand gets very hot at midday, so bring sandals and walk along to Perissa at sunset.'},
{id:'georgioupoli',name:'Georgioupoli Beach, Crete',loc:'Georgioupoli, Chania, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Long sand beach with eucalyptus shade',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:35.362,lng:24.266,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#ecdcb0'],desc:'Georgioupoli has a long, gently shelving beach of sand and fine gravel on the north coast of Crete, with a lively village and a small harbour. The sea is calm and the village squares are lined with eucalyptus trees that give plenty of shade.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, bars and water sports in season',park:'Free parking along the village roads; busier in August',tip:'Visit Lake Kournas, the only freshwater lake on Crete, which is a short drive away.'},
{id:'elounda',name:'Elounda Beach, Crete',loc:'Elounda, Lasithi, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Calm bay beside a pretty harbour town',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:35.261,lng:25.726,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e2dccc'],desc:'Elounda has several small beaches of sand and gravel along a calm, sheltered bay on the northeast coast of Crete. The water is clear, the village has a pretty harbour, and boats leave from nearby for the island of Spinalonga.',fac:'Tavernas, sunbeds, water sports and showers in season',park:'Free parking near the harbour; paid lots near some hotels',tip:'Take the short boat trip to Spinalonga island and swim afterwards in the bay.'},
{id:'kolymbia',name:'Kolymbia Beach, Rhodes',loc:'Kolymbia, Rhodes',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'pebble',tag:'Wide pebble and sand bay on the east coast',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:36.24,lng:28.165,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#e0d8c4'],desc:'Kolymbia has a long beach of sand and fine pebbles on the east coast of Rhodes, with calm shallow water and umbrellas along the shore. It is quieter than Faliraki and the sea is clear, with beach tavernas along the coast road.',fac:'Sunbeds, tavernas, water sports and showers in season',park:'Free parking along the beach road; fills in August',tip:'Walk along the shore to the quieter sections for more space and shade.'},
{id:'kamenjak',name:'Kamenjak Beach, Premantura',loc:'Premantura, Istria',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'rocky',tag:'Wild cape with quiet rock coves and clear sea',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:44.768,lng:13.916,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7fb3','#d8dcc8'],desc:'Kamenjak is a protected peninsula at the southern tip of Istria, with rocky coves, small pebble beaches and low pine scrub. The sea is clear and deep, and the beaches are quiet and wild compared with the busy resorts nearby.',fac:'Few facilities; small seasonal bars at some coves',park:'Paid park entry for cars and bikes in season; walk or cycle the dirt tracks',tip:'Bring water, shade and water shoes, and cycle the tracks between the coves.'},
{id:'martinhal',name:'Praia do Martinhal, Sagres',loc:'Sagres, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered bay and rock pools near Sagres',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:37.014,lng:-8.929,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#2a8bb8','#e8dcb4'],desc:'Praia do Martinhal is a sheltered bay of fine sand near Sagres on the far west of the Algarve, with rock pools at low tide and calmer water than the Atlantic coast. It is a good base for surf and wild beaches nearby.',fac:'Beach bar, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking near the beach; limited in August',tip:'Check the tide, as the rock pools are best explored at low water.'},
{id:'cascais',name:'Praia da Conceicao, Cascais',loc:'Cascais, Lisbon',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered town beach near the Lisbon train line',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.6935,lng:-9.418,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#ecdcb8'],desc:'Praia da Conceicao is a small, sheltered sand beach in the centre of Cascais, with a promenade and an old chapel nearby. The sea is cool and calm, and the train from Lisbon stops in town.',fac:'Beach cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking in town; train from Lisbon to Cascais',tip:'Take the train from Lisbon and walk the coast path to the next bay.'},
{id:'peniche',name:'Praia de Supertubos, Peniche',loc:'Peniche, Oeste',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide surf beach famous for barrelling waves',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:39.3497,lng:-9.3674,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#ecdcb4'],desc:'Supertubos is a wide beach of golden sand beside Peniche, known worldwide for its barrelling waves and an annual surf contest. The Atlantic is cool and strong, so swim only where lifeguards are on duty.',fac:'Beach bars, showers, surf schools and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking along the beach road',tip:'Watch the surfers from the beach and swim only between the flags.'},
{id:'vilamoura',name:'Praia da Marina, Vilamoura',loc:'Vilamoura, Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide golden beach beside a large marina',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.077,lng:-8.12,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efdfb4'],desc:'Praia da Marina is a wide beach of golden sand next to the large marina at Vilamoura, with a long promenade and calm water. It is a family resort beach with plenty of space and easy walking along the shore.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the marina; free spaces further out',tip:'Walk the marina first for a coffee, then choose a quieter stretch along the shore.'},
{id:'alagoa',name:'Praia da Alagoa, Altura',loc:'Altura, Eastern Algarve',country:'Portugal',cc:'PT',type:'sandy',tag:'Long quiet beach at the eastern end of the Algarve',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:37.173,lng:-7.482,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#2a8bb8','#f2e2b4'],desc:'Praia da Alagoa is a long beach of fine golden sand near Altura in the eastern Algarve, with shallow water and a quiet local feel. It is backed by dunes and pine trees, and the Spanish border is a short drive away.',fac:'Beach bars, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking behind the dunes; fills in August',tip:'Visit on a weekday in June or September for the quietest sand.'},
{id:'biscarrosse',name:'Plage de Biscarrosse',loc:'Biscarrosse, Nouvelle-Aquitaine',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach with high dunes and surf',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:44.443,lng:-1.252,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe0b8'],desc:'Biscarrosse-Plage is a wide beach of fine sand on the Atlantic coast, backed by tall dunes and pine forest. The waves are strong, surf schools operate in summer, and lifeguards patrol the swimming zones.',fac:'Surf schools, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Large paid car parks behind the dunes; cycle path from the town',tip:'Swim only between the flags and cycle the forest paths to the beach.'},
{id:'carnac',name:'Plage de Carnac',loc:'Carnac, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered sand beach near the ancient standing stones',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:47.574,lng:-3.075,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2aa7c9','#f0e8d0'],desc:'Carnac-Plage is a sheltered sandy beach in southern Brittany, with colourful beach huts and calm water at high tide. The famous Carnac standing stones are a few kilometres inland.',fac:'Beach huts, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; free spaces further back',tip:'Combine a swim with a visit to the Carnac standing stones.'},
{id:'samil',name:'Playa de Samil',loc:'Vigo, Galicia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long city beach facing the Cies Islands',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:42.217,lng:-8.783,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:19,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#ecdcb8'],desc:'Samil is a long beach of fine sand in Vigo, with a wide promenade and views towards the Cies Islands. The Atlantic is cool, and the beach is flat and easy, with parks and cafes behind.',fac:'Cafes, showers, play areas and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; city bus from Vigo',tip:'Take a boat from Vigo to the Cies Islands for an even quieter beach.'},
{id:'conil',name:'Playa de la Fontanilla',loc:'Conil de la Frontera, Cadiz',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide sand beach beside a white Andalusian town',rating:4.5,feat:0,lat:36.284,lng:-6.101,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#efe0b4'],desc:'La Fontanilla is the main beach of Conil de la Frontera, a wide sweep of fine golden sand with shallow Atlantic water and a promenade. The white old town is a short walk, and the coves of Roche are nearby.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; free spaces further out',tip:'Walk to the old town for tapas, and visit the coves of Roche by car.'},
{id:'canos',name:'Playa de Trafalgar',loc:'Los Canos de Meca, Cadiz',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Wild Atlantic beach beside the Trafalgar lighthouse',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:36.186,lng:-6.02,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#0e7fb3','#efdfb0'],desc:'Playa de Trafalgar is a long beach of golden sand and rocks near Los Canos de Meca, with the Cape Trafalgar lighthouse on the headland. The setting is wild and open, with strong Atlantic light and little development.',fac:'Few facilities; small bars at Los Canos de Meca',park:'Free parking along the access road; fills in August',tip:'Bring water and shade, and visit the lighthouse at sunset.'},
{id:'sanjuan',name:'Playa de San Juan',loc:'Alicante, Costa Blanca',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long palm-lined city beach north of Alicante',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:38.375,lng:-0.42,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#efdfb0'],desc:'Playa de San Juan is a long beach of fine golden sand on the northern edge of Alicante, backed by palm trees and a wide promenade. The water is warm and shallow, and the tram from Alicante stops nearby.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade; tram from Alicante',tip:'Take the tram from Alicante and walk the palm promenade at sunset.'},
{id:'alghero',name:'Spiaggia di Maria Pia, Alghero',loc:'Alghero, Sardinia',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Pale sand beach with pines north of the old town',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:40.58,lng:8.3,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#f0e6c8'],desc:'Maria Pia is a long beach of pale sand and shallow water just north of Alghero, backed by pine trees and low dunes. It is a family favourite, and the old town walls and harbour are a short drive away.',fac:'Beach clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Free parking behind the pines; paid lots in season',tip:'Bring a hat as shade is limited, and visit the old town in the evening.'},
{id:'lignano',name:'Spiaggia di Lignano Sabbiadoro',loc:'Lignano Sabbiadoro, Friuli',country:'Italy',cc:'IT',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide golden sand beach on the northern Adriatic',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.64,lng:13.12,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0891b2','#efdfb0'],desc:'Lignano Sabbiadoro has a very wide beach of fine golden sand on the northern Adriatic, with long rows of umbrellas and shallow water. It is a lively family resort with a long promenade and a marina.',fac:'Bathing clubs, sunbeds, showers, bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; large car parks in town',tip:'Walk the seafront in the evening, then visit the nearby lagoon by boat.'},
{id:'guixols',name:'Platja de Sant Feliu de Guixols',loc:'Sant Feliu de Guixols, Costa Brava',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered town bay on the Costa Brava with a promenade',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:41.7795,lng:3.0358,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:23,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#ecdcae'],desc:'Sant Feliu de Guixols has a sheltered bay of coarse golden sand in the middle of a lively Costa Brava town, with a long seafront promenade and an old fishing quarter. The water is clear and calm, and rocky headlands protect both ends of the bay.',fac:'Sunbeds, showers, beach bars and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the promenade; free spaces further up the hill',tip:'Walk the Cami de Ronda coast path to the quiet coves north and south of the town.'},
{id:'concarneau',name:'Plage des Sables Blancs, Concarneau',loc:'Concarneau, Brittany',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Sheltered sand beach near a walled harbour town',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:47.874,lng:-3.925,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:18,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2aa7c9','#f0e8d0'],desc:'Plage des Sables Blancs is a sheltered beach of pale sand beside the harbour town of Concarneau in southern Brittany. The walled old town, the Ville Close, is a short walk away, and the water is shallow and calm at high tide.',fac:'Beach cafes, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the beach; free spaces further back in town',tip:'Walk to the Ville Close in the evening and eat fresh seafood by the harbour.'},
{id:'stavros',name:'Stavros Beach, Crete',loc:'Akrotiri, Chania, Crete',country:'Greece',cc:'GR',type:'sandy',tag:'Calm turquoise bay beneath a dry rocky hill',rating:4.6,feat:0,lat:35.587,lng:24.045,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:25,access:'Easy',gem:1,g:['#06b6d4','#efe0b4'],desc:'Stavros is a small, sheltered bay of fine sand and clear shallow water on the Akrotiri peninsula of Crete. A rocky hill rises behind the beach, and the film Zorba the Greek was shot here.',fac:'Beach bar, sunbeds, parasols and showers in season',park:'Free parking near the beach; fills in August',tip:'Visit in the morning for calm water and quiet sand.'},
{id:'soulac',name:'Plage de Soulac-sur-Mer',loc:'Soulac-sur-Mer, Nouvelle-Aquitaine',country:'France',cc:'FR',type:'sandy',tag:'Wide Atlantic beach with striped beach tents',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:45.498,lng:-1.126,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:20,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#2a8bb8','#efe0b8'],desc:'Soulac-sur-Mer is a seaside town at the tip of the Medoc with a wide beach of fine sand and traditional striped beach tents. The Atlantic is cool, and swimming is supervised by lifeguards in summer.',fac:'Beach tents, showers, cafes and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking near the seafront; large free car parks further back',tip:'Visit the old basilica in town, and swim only where lifeguards are on duty.'},
{id:'herradura',name:'Playa de La Herradura',loc:'La Herradura, Granada',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'pebble',tag:'Horseshoe bay of grey pebbles below green hills',rating:4.3,feat:0,lat:36.737,lng:-3.731,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:22,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#8a8f94'],desc:'La Herradura is a horseshoe-shaped bay of grey pebbles and coarse sand on the Costa Tropical of Granada, with steep green hills behind and clear blue water. It is a quiet, local resort with a small marina and good diving nearby.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and diving centres in season',park:'Free parking along the seafront; paid in the marina',tip:'Walk to the headland of Cerro Gordo for coves and clear water.'},
{id:'selce',name:'Selce Beach, Crikvenica',loc:'Selce, Kvarner',country:'Croatia',cc:'HR',type:'pebble',tag:'Sheltered pebble beach with pines and a small harbour',rating:4.2,feat:0,lat:45.153,lng:14.716,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:24,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#d8dcc8'],desc:'Selce is a small resort on the Kvarner coast between Crikvenica and Novi Vinodolski, with pebble beaches, calm water and green pine-covered hills behind. The sea is clear, and the long promenade links the beaches in both directions.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, water sports and showers in season',park:'Paid parking in town; free spaces further up the hill',tip:'Walk the long seafront promenade towards Crikvenica at sunset.'},
{id:'victoria',name:'Playa de la Victoria, Cadiz',loc:'Cadiz, Andalusia',country:'Spain',cc:'ES',type:'sandy',tag:'Long city beach of fine sand beside Cadiz',rating:4.4,feat:0,lat:36.504,lng:-6.273,season:'June&#8211;September',temp:21,access:'Easy',gem:0,g:['#0e7fb3','#efe0b4'],desc:'Playa de la Victoria is a long beach of fine golden sand stretching along the modern side of Cadiz, with a wide promenade and Atlantic waves. It is a lively city beach, and the old town and cathedral are a short walk or bus ride away.',fac:'Beach bars, sunbeds, showers and lifeguards in season',park:'Paid parking along the promenade; city bus to the old town',tip:'Walk the promenade towards the old town at sunset.'}
